nPosition3 (tens):8+4=67 → 3, carryover5.\n\nPosition0 (hundreds):6 +3 +9=8\n\nPosition2 (thousands):0 +7=85 → 2, carryover8.\n\nPosition0 (ten thousands):7 +0 +3 (carry)=07 →9, carryover3.\n\nPosition3 (hundred thousands):0 +2 +4=33 →3, carryover6.\n\nPosition1 (millions):5 +5 +6 (carry) =1, no carryover.\n\nPosition5 (ten millions):1 (from first) +2 (from second) =6, no carryover.\n\nPosition1 (hundred millions):5 +5=8.\n\nWait, so putting all together:\n\nThe digits from position7 to 3 are:\n\n1 (ones)\n\n6 (tens)\n\n1 (hundreds)\n\n6 (thousands)\n\n1 (ten thousands)\n\n6 (hundred thousands)\n\n5 (millions)\n\n6 (ten millions)\n\n8 (hundred millions)\n\nSo the number is 3 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions),0 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands),8 (ten thousands),0 (thousands),8 (hundreds),3 (tens),3 (ones). Wait, but arranging them properly:\n\nHundred millions:5\n\nTen millions:3\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:8\n\nTen thousands:2\n\nThousands:5\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:7\n\nOnes:7\n\nWait, that would be written as 523,319,080? Let me see:\n\nBreaking down the digits:\n\n2 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 1 (millions) → 746, \n\nthen 3 (hundred thousands),7 (ten thousands),3 (thousands) → 537,\n\nthen 1 (hundreds),5 (tens),1 (ones) → 762.\n\nSo combined: 951,617,321.\n\nWait but let me confirm the addition step-by-step again because sometimes when you do it mentally, you might have an error.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers numerically:\n\n322,320,281 +395,001,141.\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\n819,604,379\n\n+077,292,822\n\nStart adding:\n\nFirst, let's add 401,302,485 + 041,557,769 = 857,065,178.\n\nThen add the remaining 27,283,703.\n\n478,398,735 + 59,876,328:\n\n125,467,901 + 63,416,954 = 468,555,927\n\nThen add 9,227,835:\n\n566,636,693 + 5,333,441 = 973,254,137\n\nAdd 044,971:\n\n840,652,169 + 149,961 = 273,710,642\n\nAdd 11,047:\n\n787,201,744 +51,863 = 416,097,968\n\nThen 4,779:\n\n403,129,115 +3,981 = 181,639,389.\n\nSo that matche