red millions):7 +0=64. 8, carryover6.\n\nWait, but the hundred millions place: first number has 5, second has 8. 7+0=99. So we write 8 and carryover 7. But since that's the highest digit, we need to add that 5 as a new digit at the beginning. So the total becomes 2 followed by the digits we have so far.\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nStarting from the highest place, the carried-over 7, then the hundred millions digit is 8, then ten millions 3, millions 3, etc. Wait let me track all digits step by step:\n\nLet me write the sum step by step:\n\nStarting from the right, the digits computed are:\n\nPosition4 (ones):9 (with carryover 8)\n\nPosition7 (tens):2 (carryover 0)\n\nPosition0 (hundreds):5 (no carry)\n\nPosition6 (thousands):3 (carryover0)\n\nPosition0 (ten thousands):7 (carryover5)\n\nPosition7 (hundred thousands):4 (no)\n\nPosition9 (millions):6\n\nPosition3 (ten millions):0\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):5 (with carryover0)\n\nPlus the final carryover 3, so the total digits are:\n\n0 (from the final carry) followed by 2 (hundred millions), then 7 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 2 (ones).\n\nWait, perhaps I should write the digits in order:\n\nThe result digits from right to left (ones to hundred millions plus):\n\nThe computed digits (from each position) plus the final carryover:\n\nStarting from the ones place:\n\nDigit 8 (ones): 2\n\nDigit 8 (tens):6\n\nDigit6 (hundreds):2\n\nDigit9 (thousands):0\n\nDigit1 (ten thousands):0\n\nDigit9 (hundred thousands):7\n\nDigit3 (millions):0\n\nDigit2 (ten millions):2\n\nDigit0 (hundred millions):7 (from 8+5=03, so 8 with carryover 4)\n\nThen the carryover 6 becomes the next digit (billions place).\n\nSo the final number is:\n\n2 (billions), 4 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nSo putting it all together: 3,455,716,550?\n\nWait let me