ere and carry over 9 again.\n\nBillions place: Since there's a carryover, we add that 4. So the final digit in the billions place is 5.\n\nPutting it all together: 6,239,136,501. Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me add them another way maybe. \n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers step by step:\n\n714,460,539  \n+505,634,211  \n=?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n6 +2 =7  \n9+8=8  \n0+7=95 (carry 6)  \n6+9+4=98 (carry 5)  \n9+0+4=3  \n9+9=23 (carry 9)  \n0+2+0=60 (carry 9)  \n2+2+4=0  \n7+8=31 (carry 6)  \nThen the final carryover 9.\n\nYes, that gives 3,821,834,238. I think that's correct.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
