\nWait, so when adding digit by digit:\n\nPosition1 (units):3+3=6\n\nPosition2 (tens):0+0=0\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1+8=9\n\nPosition4 (thousands):5+8=13 \u2192 write 3, carryover1\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):1+8 +1 (carry)=10 \u2192 write 0, carryover1\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):4+8 +1 (carry)=13 \u2192 write3, carryover1\n\nPosition7 (millions):9+3 +1 (carry)=13 \u2192 write3, carryover1\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):5+8 +1 (carry)=14 \u2192 write4, carryover1\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):8+8 +1 (carry)=17 \u2192 write7, carryover1\n\nNow, the carryover1 becomes the next digit (billions place).\n\nSo the total is 1 (billions), 7 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 6 (units). Wait, that's confusing.\n\nWait, let me list the digits from right to left (positions 1-9 plus the carryover):\n\nPositions:\n\n1:6\n\n2:0\n\n3:9\n\n4:3 (with carry 1)\n\n5:0 (since 10 was written as 0 with carryover 1)\n\nWait, let me redo the breakdown with proper carries:\n\nStarting over:\n\nPosition1: 3+3=6 \u2192 6\n\nPosition2:0+0=0 \u21920\n\nPosition3:1+8=9 \u21929\n\nPosition4:5+8=13 \u21923, carryover1\n\nPosition5:1 (from first number's ten thousands) +8 (from second's ten thousands) +1 (carry) = 10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nPosition6:4 (hundred thousands) +8 (hundred thousands) +1 (carry)=13 \u21923, carryover1\n\nPosition7:9 (millions) +3 (millions) +1 (carry)=13 \u21923, carryover1\n\nPosition8:5 (ten millions) +8 (ten millions) +1 (carry)=14 \u21924, carryover1\n\nPosition9:8 (hundred millions) +8 (hundred millions) +1 (carry)=17 \u21927, carryover1\n\nNow, the carryover1 is added as a new digit (10th position: billions).\n\nSo the digits from position1 (units) to 10 (billions) are:\n\nPosition10:1,\n\nPosition9:7,\n\nPosition8:4,\n\nPosition7:3,\n\nPosition6:3,\n\nPosition5:0,\n\nPosition4:3,\n\nPosition3:9,\n\nPosition2:0,\n\nPosition1:6.\n\nTherefore, the number is:\n\n1 (bi