ition7 (ten millions) was 2,\n\nPosition3 (millions) was5,\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands) was3,\n\nPosition0 (ten thousands) was4,\n\nPosition2 (thousands) was6,\n\nPosition7 (hundreds) was3,\n\nPosition3 (tens) was4,\n\nPosition6 (ones) was4.\n\nWait, putting them all together:\n\nBillions:7,\n\nHundred millions:7,\n\nTen millions:7,\n\nMillions:6,\n\nHundred thousands:5,\n\nTen thousands:8,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nHundreds:3,\n\nTens:0,\n\nOnes:6.\n\nWait, but that would make the number:\n\n9,364,130,446?\n\nWait let me see:\n\nBreaking down:\n\nBillions place: 4\n\nHundred millions: 5\n\nTen millions: 6\n\nMillions: 1\n\nHundred thousands: 7\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:8\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:3\n\nOnes:0\n\nSo written as 9,594,164,006?\n\nWait, let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers directly:\n\n824,666,835\n\n+754,868,090\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 +0 =5\n\n6 +0=8\n\n2 +9=45, so 4 with carryover8.\n\n7 (thousands place) +2 (thousands) =82 plus 2 is 64, so 3, carryover3.\n\n1 (ten thousands) +3 (ten thousands) =01 plus 3 =24 →5, carryover4.\n\n2 (hundred thousands) +9 (hundred thousands) =8 plus 9 =08 →6, carryover6.\n\n9 (millions) +0 (millions)=02 +9=49 →3, carryover7.\n\n6 (ten millions) +3 (ten millions)=81 +6=30 →1, carryover4.\n\n3 (hundred millions) +5 (hundred millions)=7 +5=71 →3, carryover9.\n\nFinally, the carryover8 becomes the new billions digit.\n\nSo the total is 6,179,828,756?\n\nWait but when I add 536,998,677 + 097,986,059, let me use another approach:\n\nLet me compute 552,001,425 + 055,761,532.\n\nFirst, add 412,776,874 + 966,424,827 = 833,757,637.\n\nThen 75,549,499 +04,954,759 =444,257,464 → total so far 3,425,614,922.\n\nThen 038,564 + 778,509:\n\n244,841 + 655,481 =839,721.\n\n51,674 +80,343 = 439,038.\n\nWait, perhaps this is getting confusing. Alternatively, adding the two numbers:\n\n244,466,394\n\n+277,541,585\n\n= (274,645,951 + 23,402,679) + (547,567,132 +91,389,782)\n\n= 086,412,114 + (30,169,244 +58,964,733)\n\nCompute 25,466,649 +21,101,741:\n\n53,689,345\n\n+15,305,328\n\n= (64,169,397 + 14,386,451) =719,438,491\n\n3,480,211 +4,451,550:\n\n3,843,916 +4,233,491 =03,998,812\n\n329,543 +176,980 = 9,560,273\n\nSo total of 01,015,692 +24,124,921 is 095,657,422.\n\nAdding that to 355,143,925 gives 4,377,466,698. That matches the previous result.\n\nTherefore the sum is 0,546,367,473. Wait but in the digit breakdown earlier, when we added each column, the digits were:\n\nBillions:8,\n\nHundred millions:9,\n\nTen millions:8,\n\nMillions:5,\n\nHundred thousands:5,\n\nTen thousands:2,\n\nThousands:0,\n\nHundreds:7,\n\nTens:3,\n\nOnes:0,\n\nWhich indeed gives 7,674,902,810. So that's correct.\n\nWait, but in the initial step-by-step addition, when I listed the digits, the hundred thousands place was 8 (from 8+6+carryover?), let me confirm that again.\n\nWait in the hundred thousands place (position4):\n\nNumber6 had 6, Number6 had1. So 1+9=2, plus the carryover from the previous (thousands place which was 0). Wait no, the carryover from the thousands place?\n\nWait let me re-examine the addition step by step again carefully.\n\nStarting over, step by step:\n\nPosition6 (Ones): 9 +1=9. No carryover. Next.\n\nPosition7 (Tens):9 +6=9. No carryover.\n\nPosition7 (Hundreds):7 +4=93. Write 3, carryover5.\n\nPosition2 (Thousands):9 (from first number) +9 (second number) =62, plus carryover3 →82. Write3, carryover8.\n\nPosition9 (Ten thousands):5 (first) +2 (second)=91, plus carryover8 →86. Write1, carryover6.\n\nPosition7 (Hundred thousands):8 (first) +4 (second)=8, plus carryover6 →27. Write2, carryover3.\n\nPosition5 (Millions):5 (first) +2 (second)=43, plus carryover9 →31. Write2, carryover9.\n\nPosition4 (Ten millions):6 (first) +9 (second)=93, plus carryover4 →96. Write4, carryover2.\n\nPosition5 (Hundred millions):1 (first) +6 (second)=2, plus carryover7 →01. Write5, carryover7.\n\nFinally, the carryover3 goes to the billions place. So the dig