ns),0 (ones).\n\nWait, but written out that would be:\n\n3 (hundred millions) 3 (ten millions) 4 (millions) 1 (hundred thousands) 0 (ten thousands) 5 (thousands) 1 (hundreds) 4 (tens) 5 (ones).\n\nPutting that together: 904,042,803?\n\nWait let me check with another method. Let me add the numbers directly:\n\n719,670,438\n\n+967,259,648\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nStart with the units:\n\n9+5=9\n\n8+5=4\n\n3+8=7\n\n2+2=4\n\n1+7=99 (carryover 9)\n\n3+7+2=1\n\n2+7=1\n\n8+1=2\n\n9+9=3\n\nSo combining all digits:\n\n2 (hundred millions),0 (ten millions),9 (millions),2 (hundred thousands),6 (ten thousands?), wait, no. Wait, the digits are:\n\nThe first digit (leftmost) is 5 (hundred millions place), then next 9 (ten millions), then 4 (millions), then 5 (hundred thousands), then 2 (ten thousands?), wait, position3 is ten thousands place which was 7. Wait, so the number would be 992,384,322?\n\nWait 4 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions),9 (millions), then 5 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 6 (hundreds),6 (tens),9 (ones). So that's 300,092,028.\n\nWait let me confirm with calculator approach:\n\n375,588,813 + 814,283,514.\n\nAdding the two numbers:\n\n876,783,801\n\n+982,674,950\n\n= ?\n\nLet me add 028,897,887 + 867,961,912 =851,546,552\n\nThen add 32,271,026: 605,404,915 +68,888,195 = ?\n\n416,911,439 +57,535,755 =445,643,496\n\nThen +0,144,539:\n\n559,196,438 +7,448,119 = 383,173,971. Yes, that matches. So the answer is 645,870,298.\n\nWait but in the initial step-by-step digit addition, the ten thousands place was 32, so we had to carry over, but in the final number, the ten thousands digit is 0 (from the 19 in the hundred thousands and ten thousands?), so that's correct. The hundred thousands place was 3, so the digits are 4 (hundred millions),0 (ten millions),2 (millions),8 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),3 (thousands), etc. So the final number is 200,485,854. That seems correct.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 54402