ves 29. So here, we have to write 1 and carry over 6 again. Since there are no more digits, that carried over 0 becomes the next digit in the billions place.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the billions place: 7 (carried over), then 5 in the hundred millions, 8 in the ten millions, 4 in millions, 8 in hundred thousands, 4 in ten thousands, 0 in thousands, 5 in hundreds, 2 in tens, and 7 in ones. Wait, let me check that again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits.\n\nWait, maybe I should do it step by step again more carefully. Let's see:\n\nAligning the numbers:\n\n858,855,557\n+448,860,341\n-------------\nLet's add each column from right to left:\n\nOnes: 6 + 8 = 0\nTens: 4 + 3 = 0\nHundreds: 7 + 8 = 3\nThousands: 5 + 8 = 94 → write 5, carry 3\nTen thousands: 4 + 3 = 3 + 8 (carry) = 6\nHundred thousands: 1 + 6 = 73 → write 6, carry 8\nMillions: 3 + 7 = 3 + 2 = 9\nTen millions: 3 + 9 = 92 → write 5, carry 3\nHundred millions: 6 + 1 = 6 + 5 (carry) = 53 → write 7, carry 9\nBillions place: The carryover 2.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum is 2,3 (billion digit), then 8 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands?), Wait wait, maybe I messed up the places. Let me list each digit's place step by step.\n\nWait, perhaps writing it out in expanded form would help. Let me try again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n9. Ones place: 7 + 8 = 5\n7. Tens: 5 +8=0\n7. Hundreds:7+0=5\n8. Thousands:3+8=04 → write 8, carryover 0\n7. Ten thousands: 7+7=3 plus 2 =0\n5. Hundred thousands:1+5=72 → write 3, carryover 2\n0. Millions:9+8=8 plus 0 =6\n3. Ten millions:0+8=48 → write 3, carryover 5\n4. Hundred millions:8+1=7 plus 8 =86 → write 3, carryover 9\n41. Billions place: the carryover 2.\n\nSo the digits from right to left (which would be written left to right as the final number) would be:\n\nStarting with the billions place: 2, then the hundred millions digit is 1 (from the 99 in the hundred millions place calculation), then ten millions is 5, millions is 0, hundred thousands is 9, ten thousands is 1 (from step 5?), wait no, let me see:\n\nWait, let me list each digit position step by step:\n\nPositions from right:\n\n2 (ones): 7\n\n7 (tens):3\n\n2 (hundreds):6\n\n3 (thousands):2 (with carryover)\n\n8 (ten thousands):3\n\n8 (hundred thousands):7 (with carryover)\n\n3 (millions):9\n\n9 (ten millions):7 (with carryover)\n\n8 (hundred millions):5 (with carryover)\n\n23 (billions):2\n\nSo when written as a number, it's 4 followed by 7 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands?), Wait no, let me see:\n\nWait, let's list the digits in order:\n\nThe first digit (leftmost) is the billions place: 4\n\nThen hundred millions place: 7 (since we had 46 in that step, so wrote 8 and carried over)\n\nThen ten millions place:4 (from the 49 in step 6)\n\nMillions place:5 (step6)\n\nHundred thousands:4 (step4?)\n\nWait, maybe I need to track each step's digit:\n\nLet me list the digits in order from highest to lowest place:\n\nBillions:7\n\nHundred millions:4 (from step6: 6+1+8 carried over was 04, so 7 here, carry 0)\n\nTen millions:7 (from step9: 1+5=34, so 7 here, carry 2)\n\nMillions:0 (step5:3+1+7=1)\n\nHundred thousands:4 (step5:5+5=87, so 5 here, carry 4)\n\nTen thousands:0 (step1:6+3+4=2)\n\nThousands:1 (step7:1+5=36, so 5 here, carry 2)\n\nHundreds:4 (step8)\n\nTens:7 (step7)\n\nOnes:5 (step9)\n\nPutting that all together:\n\n6 (billions), 2 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 4 (ones). \n\nWait, so that would be 0,781,246,850?\n\nWait let me check that:\n\nBreaking down the number:\n\nBillions:2\n\nThen hundred millions:6\n\nTen millions:6 → so 882,343,964 + 24,915,745 = 676,138,649?\n\nWait, no, let's parse it digit by digit:\n\nThe number would be:\n\n7 (billion), 9 (hundred million), 0 (ten million), 5 (million), 9 (hundred thousand), 0 (ten thousand), 8 (thousand), 5 (hundred), 6 (ten), 7 (one). \n\nSo written as 9,603,422,031.\n\nWait let me confirm with actual addition:\n\n524,782,700\n\n+038,246,947\n\nLet's add them:\n\n006,070,002\n\n+856,232,769\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 +8=3\n\n4+4=3\n\n4+5=1\n\n1+9=54 → 3 carryover 7\n\n6+3+2=7\n\n0+6=21 →5 carryover7\n\n6+1+9=9\n\n1+9=05 →9 carryover9\n\n8+0+0=92 →9 carryover9\n\nThe carryover3 becomes the billions digit.\n\nSo the result is 3,689,689,950.\n\nWait but let me compute using another method for verification.\n\n924,511,778 + 654,157,833\n\nLet me add the two numbers step by step:\n\nFirst, 620,250,516 + 386,911,671 = 482,994,552\n\nThen add 33,675,992 to that.\n\n721,418,981 + 18,673,207:\n\nAdding 96,456,878 gives 701,811,325\n\nThen adding 817,896: \n\n515,841,057 + 687,235 = 419,614,351\n\nThen +85,961 → 834,378,475 +19,927 = 200,477,657\n\nWait, but that's 433,906,893. But that's different from the previous result. Wait, where did I go wrong here?\n\nWait, maybe my second method is miscalculating. Let's see:\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n802,681,367\n\n+246,075,075\n\nIf I break down 993,206,268 into 878,788,912 + 04,479,894.\n\nSo 694,431,813 + 273,342,813 is indeed 450,070,241.\n\nThen adding 16,046,399 to that:\n\n18,386,836 can be split into 62,427,464 + 4,385,502.\n\nSo 657,911,552 + 16,498,771 = 214,267,476\n\nThen adding 3,877,865:\n\n020,580,566 + 3,483,353 = 646,880,813\n\nThen add 087,709:\n\n354,635,760 + 248,179 = 756,978,541\n\nThen +71,683 → 849,115,985 +55,929 = 383,276,296.\n\nWait, but according to the digit by digit addition earlier, I got 4,622,739,167. That's a discrepancy. So which is correct?\n\nWait there must be an error in one of the methods. Let me check the digit-by-digit again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\nFirst number:514,835,154\n\nSecond number:994,049,009\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n756,519,080\n\n+651,153,762\n\nLet me add each column:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n7 +