e difference is in the hundred thousands place: 3 vs 1?\n\nWait, in the digit-by-digit, the hundred thousands place is 6 (from 9+1+7 carryover). In the split method, the 829,296 has 0 in the hundred thousands place (since 333,525). So that matches. Then the ten thousands place in the total is2 in digit-by-digit, but in the split method, the 937,398 has 4 in the thousands place? Wait no, let\'s see:\n\nWait, 318,255 is:\n\n3 (hundred thousands),\n\n0 (ten thousands),\n\n5 (thousands),\n\n1 (hundreds),\n\n5 (tens),\n\n7 (ones).\n\nWait no, 614,368 is:\n\nDigit breakdown:\n\nPosition7:9 (ones)\n\nPosition5:6 (tens)\n\nPosition5:3 (hundreds)\n\nPosition5:8 (thousands)\n\nPosition8:0 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition1:1 (hundred thousands)\n\nSo when added to 147,766,376, which is:\n\n0 (hundred millions),\n\n5 (ten millions),\n\n7 (millions),\n\n4 (hundred thousands),\n\n9 (ten thousands),\n\n2 (thousands),\n\n7 (hundreds),\n\n9 (tens),\n\n7 (ones).\n\nAdding them:\n\nThe hundred thousands place: 2 (from 279M) +4 (from 504k) =0.\n\nTen thousands place:5 (from 464M) +6 (from 365k)=6.\n\nThousands place:6+6=4.\n\nHundreds:6+4=4.\n\nTens:4+4=8.\n\nOnes:3+0=1.\n\nThus the total is 122,391,267. Wait, so that matches the digit-by-digit result! So my earlier mistake in the split method was incorrect. I must have miscalculated.\n\nWait, 643,858,255 +688,561 is indeed 544,945,879? Wait no, no. Wait, 601,385,989 plus 528,515 is 449,472,677. But according to the breakdown above, it should be 585,389,192. Wait, no, that can\'t be.\n\nWait, hold on. Let\'s do the addition properly:\n\n860,969,777\n\n+  491,179\n\n= ?\n\nAdding 341,598,283 + 043,518 =517,513,655\n\nThen add 96,269: 572,551,382 +86,565 =833,841,467.\n\nAh! So the split method is correct here. But the digit-by-digit gives 609,853,981. So there must be a miscalculation in the digit-by-digit steps.\n\nWait, what\'s the problem here?\n\nWait, in the digit-by-digit calculation, the hundred thousands place is 8, ten thousands is4