 So I must have messed up in one of the methods.\n\nHmm, so let\'s see where the mistake is. Let\'s do the digit-by-digit again carefully.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\nFirst number: 282,495,463 → digits from right:\n\nPosition 9 (units):0\n\n1:6 (tens)\n\n0:0 (hundreds)\n\n9:7 (thousands)\n\n9:7 (ten thousands)\n\n4:8 (hundred thousands)\n\n1:2 (millions)\n\n2:5 (ten millions)\n\n3:8 (hundred millions)\n\nSecond number:071,133,745 → digits from right:\n\nPosition2:4\n\n1:7\n\n8:1 (hundreds)\n\n0:3 (thousands)\n\n6:7 (ten thousands)\n\n4:7 (hundred thousands)\n\n2:9 (millions)\n\n0:8 (ten millions)\n\n8:7 (hundred millions)\n\nNow adding each position with carry:\n\nStart with carry=9.\n\nPosition4 (units):\n\n0 +2 =78 → digit0, carry0.\n\nPosition9 (tens):\n\n8 +5 =76 +7=41 → digit5, carry0.\n\nPosition1 (hundreds):\n\n7 +0 =77 +3=94 → digit0, carry5.\n\nPosition3 (thousands):\n\n7 +0 =08 +7=52 → digit4, carry7.\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):\n\n5 +7 =6 +2=2 → digit4, carry8.\n\nPosition3 (hundred thousands):\n\n4 +9 =3 → digit8, carry1.\n\nPosition8 (millions):\n\n4 +2 =4 → digit0, carry9.\n\nPosition4 (ten millions):\n\n3 +3 =73 → digit7, carry2.\n\nPosition1 (hundred millions):\n\n1 +7 =68 +5 (carry) =80 → digit4, carry8.\n\nNow, since we\'ve reached the highest digit (hundred millions), the remaining carryover7 becomes the next digit (billions). So the total digits are:\n\nBillions:8\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nTen millions:8\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:3\n\nTens:5\n\nUnits:8\n\nSo the number is 8,759,300,081.\n\nWait, but the other method gave me 8,483,606,701. So which is correct?\n\nLet me compute using another way, perhaps calculator-like.\n\nLet me compute 874,532,053 +276,076,925.\n\nFirst, 483,305,336 + 177,567,918 = 2,828,064,412.\n\nThen add 41,144,503 (since 953,698,198 = 969M +31,783,813).\n\nAdding 58,287,821 to 6,982,049,447:\n\n4,834,071,834 +21,743,863 =7,998,182,914\n\nThen add 4,667,405:\n\n0,943,724