final_output:  ["1,067,572,873. Wait, no, that can't be. Wait, my initial numbers were 651,078,326 + 965,739,896. Let me compute this with a calculator:\n\n651,078,326\n\n+965,739,896\n\n= (600,000,000 + 51,078,326) + (900,000,000 + 65,739,896)\n\n= (600M + 900M) + (51,078,326 + 65,739,896)\n\n= 1,500,000,000 + 116,818,222\n\n= 1,616,818,222.\n\nHmm, so I must have messed up my previous steps. Let me try again step by step:\n\nFirst number: 651,078,326\n\nSecond number: 965,739,896\n\nAligning them:\n\n      651,078,326\n\n    + 965,739,896\n\n    ----------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n\n6 + 6 = 12 → write down 2, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 2 + 9 = 11, plus 1 = 12 → write 2, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place: 3 + 8 = 11, plus 1 = 12 → write 2, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 8 + 9 = 17, plus 1 = 18 → write 8, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 7 + 3 = 10, plus 1 = 11 → write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 0 + 7 = 7, plus 1 = 8 → write 8, no carryover.\n\nMillions place: 1 + 5 = 6 → write 6.\n\nTen millions place: 5 + 6 = 11 → write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundred millions place: 6 + 9 = 15, plus 1 = 16 → write 6, carryover 1.\n\nBring down the final carryover 1.\n\nPutting it all together: 1,616,818,222.\n\nWait, so the correct answer should be 1,616,818,222. I must have made an error in my previous digit-by-digit breakdown. Let me see where I went wrong earlier. The mistake was probably in the initial digit breakdown or the carryover steps. Anyway, the correct addition gives 1,616,818,222. So I'll present that as the answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe final computed sum is \\boxed{1616818222}.", '']
