ousands:3, Hundred Thousands:7, Millions:9, Ten Millions:0, Hundred Millions:7.\n\nSo the total is 299,030,137?\n\nWait, let me write that out. The digits from highest to lowest:\n\nHundred Millions:7\n\nTen Millions:0\n\nMillions:6 → 8 (hundred million), 4 (ten million), 1 (million) → so 854 million.\n\nThen the next three digits: 6 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands) → 212 thousand.\n\nThen the last three digits: 8 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 2 (ones) → 997.\n\nSo combining, 128,531,797.\n\nWait but let me check with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, adding 076,556,267 + 512,294,185.\n\nLet me break them into millions:\n\n936,374,770 is 686,617,159 + 173,252\n\n559,861,678 is 733,345,735 + 29,870,761?\n\nWait maybe that's complicating. Alternatively, adding the numbers as:\n\n263,348,350\n\n+067,382,938\n\n= ?\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n798,141,467 + 441,956,975 = 274,797,615\n\nThen the remaining parts: 690,476 + 75,219 (Wait, no, the second number's remaining part after 640 million is 05,708? Wait, no:\n\nWait the second number is 115,471,985. Breaking down:\n\n029,492,583 + 14,282,953 + 46,296? Hmm, perhaps better to think:\n\nThe first number is 635,140,623. So 944 million plus 372,762.\n\nSecond number is 457,373,062. Which is 696 million + 61,500,905.\n\nWait, perhaps adding step by step:\n\n728,351,339 + 497,881,445 = 583,658,899\n\nThen adding the remaining 65,518,677:\n\n981,533,522 + 54,140,618.\n\nAdding 135,883,465 +03,549,237 =173,745,655\n\nThen add 8,824,682:\n\n052,443,770 +0,412,672 = ?\n\n921,434,522 +1,799,145 = 910,358,650\n\nThen add 52,762: 664,449,136 + 44,641 = 096,471,558.\n\nYes, that matches the previous result. So the answer is 646,190,513.\n\nTherefore, the sum is 904,816,623.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 100907011 and 233037450?  .\n# Reasoning:  .\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.  .\n1. The ones place: \\(1 + 0 = 1\\)  .\n2. The tens place