gether:\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nTen millions:9\n\nMillions:8\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:0\n\nOnes:1\n\nThus the total is 798,016,001.\n\nBut let's check with another method:\n\n697,954,550 + 100,000,000 = 797,954,550\n\nThen add 4,161,451:\n\n797,954,550 +4,161,451 = 802,116,001? Wait that's different. There's inconsistency here.\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the positions. Let's do the addition step-by-step:\n\n697,954,550\n\n+104,161,451\n\n-------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 0 +1 =1\n\nTens:5 +5 =10 → write 0, carry1\n\nHundreds:5 +4 =9 +1=10 → write0, carry1\n\nThousands:4 (first's thousands) +1 (second's thousands) =5 +1=6 → write6, carry0\n\nTen thousands:5 (first's ten thousands) +6 (second's ten thousands) =11 → write1, carry1\n\nHundred thousands:9 (first's hundred thousands) +4 (second's hundred thousands) =13 +1 (carry)=14 → write4, carry1\n\nMillions:7 (first's millions) +0 (second's millions) =7 +1 (carry) =8 → write8, carry0\n\nTen millions:9 (first's ten millions) +0 (second's ten millions) =9 → write9, carry0\n\nHundred millions:6 (first's hundred millions) +1 (second's hundred millions) =7 → write7, carry0.\n\nSo combining all digits:\n\n7 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 1 (ones). So that's 798,016,001.\n\nWait but 697,954,550 +104,161,451 = ?\n\nLet me compute using another method:\n\n697,954,550\n\n+104,161,451\n\n= (697,000,000 + 954,550) + (104,000,000 + 161,451)\n\n= (697,000,000 + 104,000,000) + (954,550 +161,451)\n\n= 801,000,000 + 1,116,001\n\n= 802,116,001.\n\nWait, so there's a discrepancy here. Where is the mistake?\n\nAh! I see now. The second number is 104,161,451, which is 104 million, so:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n104,161,451 is 100,000,000 +4,000,000 +100,000 +60,000 +1,000 +400 +50 +1.\n\nSo when adding to 697,954,550:\n\n697,954,550\n\n+104,161,451\n\n= (697,000,000