Position3:7, Position2:9, Position0:6, Position5:6.\n\nWait, but arranging them properly, the sum would be:\n\nStarting from the highest digit (hundred millions place):\n\n5 (hundred millions)\n\nthen ten millions:6 (from Position7)\n\nmillions:4\n\nhundred thousands:9\n\nten thousands:9\n\nthousands:4\n\nhundreds:1\n\ntens:4\n\nunits:6.\n\nWait, perhaps better to write the number as:\n\n7 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions?), Wait no. Let me think again.\n\nWait the positions are:\n\nPosition7: 5 (hundred millions)\n\nPosition0: 1 (ten millions)\n\nPosition9:7 (millions)\n\nPosition2:7 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition4:2 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition1:7 (thousands)\n\nPosition9:4 (hundreds)\n\nPosition0:1 (tens)\n\nPosition6:0 (units)\n\nSo the number is:\n\n3 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 8 (units).\n\nSo putting that together: 151,748,411?\n\nWait let me check again:\n\nWait, if the digits from left to right (starting with hundred millions) are 5, 7, 1, 0, 2, 8, 0, 8, 4.\n\nBreaking into groups:\n\nHundred millions:0\n\nTen millions:1\n\nMillions:5 → so 231, (million part)\n\nThen hundred thousands:6 → 608, (thousands part?)\n\nWait maybe better to separate:\n\n1 (hundred millions)\n\n4 (ten millions)\n\n1 (millions) → so 070,698,961?\n\nThen the next digits:\n\nHundred thousands place is 2 → 252,243,\n\nten thousands 5 → 31,257,\n\nthousands 8 → 3,864,\n\nhundreds 9 → 542,\n\ntens 2,\n\nunits 8.\n\nAdding those together: 490,296,319 + 712,593 = 434,312,474; plus 63,776 → 131,263,469; plus 2,868 → 199,420,268; plus 195 → 322,953,171; plus 5 → 875,948,418.\n\nYes, so the total sum is 521,776,151.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another method. Maybe adding the numbers step by step.\n\nFirst number:048,773,846\n\nSecond number:634,210,794\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n212,193,501 is 274,739,721\n\n827,390,857 is 587,370,639\n\nAdding:\n\n741,