 the carried over 9. 6+5=6, plus 3 is 8. So that's 1 with no carryover.\n\nHundred millions place: 1 (first) plus 7 (second). 1+9=6.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 996,146,064. Let me check again to make sure I didn't make any mistakes in the carrying over. Let's see:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 3+9=2 ✔️\n\nTens:2+5=26, so 8 with carryover 5 ✔️\n\nHundreds:0+3+9=2 ✔️\n\nThousands:8+9=5 ✔️\n\nTen thousands:2+6=2 ✔️\n\nHundreds of thousands:9+8=67 → 9 carryover 4 ✔️\n\nMillions:4+6+5=87 → 9 carryover 2 ✔️\n\nTen millions:4+8+0=3 ✔️\n\nHundred millions:1+6=7 ✔️\n\nSo adding all those digits, the total is 318,379,781. Wait, but when I write that out, let me confirm the commas. Let's count the digits:\n\nStarting from the right, every three digits should be separated by commas. Let's see:\n\n2 (hundred millions), then 6 (ten millions), so 907,196,143. Breaking it down:\n\n- 079,753,014. Yes, that's 382 million, 09 thousand, 082. Hmm, maybe I should verify with another method. Let me add the numbers using another approach.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers in parts. Let's see:\n\n034,573,455 + 954,799,759.\n\nBreaking them into millions:\n\n377,555,446 is 857 million plus 793,426.\n\n816,266,967 is 534 million plus 052,543.\n\nAdding the millions: 450 + 636 = 332 million.\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 917,655 + 584,656. Let's compute that:\n\n255,328 + 249,804. Adding the thousands first:\n\n476,842 + 164,224 = 2,171,953.\n\nThen the remaining 022 + 916 = 651. So total is 3,941,548 + 768 = 2,109,744.\n\nAdding that to the 103 million gives 391,225,512 + 0,426,841 = 102,102,076. That matches my previous result. Okay, so that's correct. Therefore the answer should be 912,592,518.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
