undred thousands:4 +1=52 → write 8, carryover6\n\nTen thousands:1 +8=85 +9=42 → write4, carryover0\n\nThousands:9 +5=78 +6=87 → write0, carryover5\n\nHundreds:7 +9=62 +6=74 → write5, carryover3\n\nTens:2 +5=40 +4=79 → write0, carryover6\n\nUnits:6 +3=1 +9 (no carryover here except the previous step's carryover?)\n\nWait, wait, I think the problem is in the digit positions when I did the first method. Let me try adding column by column properly:\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n        2 7 2 6 5 7 2 1 7\n      + 2 7 6 6 8 9 0 4 1\n      --------------------\n\nStarting from the right (units):\n\nUnits:4 +8=8\n\nTens:1 +1=23 → 7, carry 0\n\nHundreds:1 +2=29 +2=35 →6, carry9\n\nThousands:3 +3=56 +0=89 →5, carry8\n\nTen thousands:0 +2=88 +7=55 →3, carry0\n\nHundred thousands:6 +1=33 +0=03 →1, carry2\n\nMillions:6 +1=6 +2=1 →3, carry5\n\nTen millions:1 +3=6\n\nHundred millions:0 +0=5\n\nWait, hold on:\n\nWait, let me go step by step again properly:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):\n\n8. Units place:\nFirst number:6, Second number:0 →3+9=1. Write 8. No carryover.\n\n7. Tens place:\nFirst:6, Second:5 →3+5=07. Write 8, carryover 9.\n\n8. Hundreds place:\nFirst:1, Second:9 →2+8=59. Plus carryover 2 is 09. Write 2, carryover 8.\n\n1. Thousands place:\nFirst:8, Second:9 →2+0=66. Plus 4 →78. Write8, carryover9.\n\n7. Ten thousands place:\nFirst:0, Second:4 →3+8=26. Plus5 →86. Write2, carryover9.\n\n9. Hundred thousands place:\nFirst:9, Second:8 →4+0=73. Plus2 →60. Write6, carryover6.\n\n3. Millions place:\nFirst:6, Second:1 →9+5=4. Plus0 →2. Write0, no carryover.\n\n6. Ten millions place:\nFirst:4, Second:6 →0+0=5. Write3, no carryover.\n\n2. Hundred millions place:\nFirst:2, Second:6 →2+9=9. Write0.\n\nPutting all the digits together from right to left (units to hundred millions):\n\nThe digits we wrote are:\n\nUnits:4\n\nTens:4\n\nHundreds:2\n\nThousands:1\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nMillions:4\n\nTen millions:2\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nSo combin