The final digits are:\n\nPosition8:5\n\nPosition7:3\n\nPosition6:0\n\nPosition5:4\n\nPosition4:3\n\nPosition3:7\n\nPosition2:3\n\nPosition1:5\n\nPosition0:2.\n\nWait, let me list them in order from highest to lowest:\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):5\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):3\n\nPosition6 (millions):0?\n\nWait position6 is millions place. The digit there was 0 from the addition? Wait, position6 was:\n\nFirst number's millions digit (position6) is7, second number's is2. 7+2+1 (carry from previous) =10, so digit0 and carry1 to next position (ten millions).\n\nSo the millions digit is0. So the number is:\n\nHundred millions:5\n\nTen millions:3 (from position7: ten millions place: 0+2+1=3)\n\nMillions:0 (position6)\n\nHundred thousands:4 (position5)\n\nTen thousands:3 (position4)\n\nThousands:7 (position3)\n\nHundreds:3 (position2)\n\nTens:5 (position1)\n\nOnes:2 (position0).\n\nTherefore, the number is 530,437,352? Wait:\n\n5 (hundred millions) → 500,000,000\n\n3 (ten millions) →30,000,000 → total 530,000,000\n\n0 (millions) →0\n\n4 (hundred thousands) →400,000 → total 530,400,000\n\n3 (ten thousands) →30,000 → 530,430,000\n\n7 (thousands) →7,000 →530,437,000\n\n3 (hundreds) →300 →530,437,300\n\n5 (tens) →50 →530,437,350\n\n2 (ones) →2 →530,437,352.\n\nWait but the original numbers were 207,512,855 and 322,924,497.\n\nAdding them:\n\n207,512,855\n\n+322,924,497\n\n=?\n\nLet me compute 207,512,855 + 322,924,497:\n\n200,000,000 + 300,000,000 =500,000,000\n\n7,512,855 +22,924,497 =30,437,352\n\nSo total is 530,437,352. Which matches the digit-by-digit result. So the correct answer is 530,437,352. Wait but the user's question was 207512855 and 322924497, which are the same as 207,512,855 and 322,924,497. So the sum is indeed 530,437,352.\n\nBut the assistant's previous thought process had some errors, but the final correct answer is 530,437,352.\n\nWait let me confirm with another method:\n\n207,512,855\n\n+322,924,497\n\n= (200,000,000 + 7,512,855) + (300,000,000 +22,