undreds:3\n- Tens:4\n- Ones:2\n\nSecond number:849,938,226:\n\n- Hundred millions:5\n- Ten millions:8\n- Millions:7\n- Hundred thousands:5\n- Ten thousands:6\n- Thousands:2\n- Hundreds:0\n- Tens:9\n- Ones:8\n\nSo when adding, the places should align as follows:\n\nLet me write them vertically by place:\n\nHundred millions: 6 + 7 = ?\n\nTen millions:6 +1 = ?\n\nMillions:6 +0 = ?\n\nHundred thousands:6 +4 = ?\n\nTen thousands:6 +1 = ?\n\nThousands:3 +7 = ?\n\nHundreds:6 +0 = ?\n\nTens:9 +9 = ?\n\nOnes:1 +3 = ?\n\nWait, but addition is done from the right (ones) to the left (hundred millions). Let me do step by step:\n\nStarting with the ones place:\n\nOnes: 9 +9 =95 → 7, carryover 3\n\nTens:9 +7 =37 +0 (carry) →58 →5, carryover5\n\nHundreds:9 +1 =90 +6 →79 →8, carryover8\n\nThousands:1 +4 +5=6 →5, no carryover\n\nTen thousands:3 +9 =8 →3\n\nHundred thousands:9 +4 =82 →0, carryover0\n\nMillions:9 +6 +8(carry)=9 →1\n\nTen millions:7 +6 =55 →6, carryover8\n\nHundred millions:5 +9 +5(carry)=71 →6, carryover6\n\nBut wait, since we've reached the hundred millions place and there's a carryover, we need to add a new digit at the billions place.\n\nSo the total sum would be:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:5\n\nTens:2\n\nHundreds:3\n\nThousands:0\n\nTen thousands:8\n\nHundred thousands:1\n\nMillions:6\n\nTen millions:7\n\nHundred millions:3\n\nPlus the carryover 2 to the billions place: 7\n\nSo putting it all together, the digits from right to left (ones to billions):\n\nOnes:6\n\nTens:3\n\nHundreds:7\n\nThousands:7\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nHundred thousands:3\n\nMillions:1\n\nTen millions:8\n\nHundred millions:2\n\nBillions:3\n\nSo writing the number from billions down to ones:\n\nBillions place:7\n\nHundred millions:3\n\nTen millions:5\n\nMillions:8\n\nHundred thousands:1\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:9\n\nTherefore, the sum is 7,175,194,904? Wait, let me verify that.\n\nWait, let me list each place with the computed digits:\n\nBillions:0