\nContinuing:\n\n- Hundred thousands place:4 +1=98 → digit2, carryover7.\n\n- Ten thousands place:6 +9=2, no carryover.\n\n- Thousands place:1 +8=4, plus carryover from hundreds place? Wait the thousands place: first number's thousands digit is8, second's thousands digit is8. So 8+9=5, plus any carryover from hundreds place. Wait the hundreds place was 6+3=50, so carryover 7 to thousands place. So thousands total is2+0 (carryover)=3, so that's correct.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to write all the steps again in order:\n\nLet me structure this step by step, writing each digit's sum and carryover:\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\n3. Ones place: 5 +2 =6 → digit3, carryover9.\n\n4. Tens place:3 +1 =8 → digit9, carryover6.\n\n0. Hundreds place:2 +0 =38 → digit9, carryover9.\n\n8. Thousands place:7 +2 =8, plus carryover4 →2 → digit5, carryover6.\n\n9. Ten thousands place:5 +3 =5 → digit8, carryover8.\n\n3. Hundred thousands place:5 +8 =72 → digit9, carryover4.\n\n9. Millions place:1 +0 =6, plus carryover8 →0 → digit0, carryover7.\n\n4. Ten millions place:7 +4 =0 → digit4, carryover2.\n\n0. Hundred millions place:3 +0 =9 → digit8, carryover7.\n\nSo compiling all the digits from the right (ones to hundred millions):\n\nOnes:0\n\nTens:6\n\nHundreds:0\n\nThousands:5\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nHundred thousands:6\n\nMillions:0\n\nTen millions:6\n\nHundred millions:2\n\nSo arranging them from highest to lowest place value:\n\nHundred millions (digit4), Ten millions (2), Millions (8), Hundred thousands (6), Ten thousands (6), Thousands (3), Hundreds (7), Tens (7), Ones (2).\n\nSo the number is 0 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands),1 (thousands),3 (hundreds),4 (tens),3 (ones).\n\nPutting that together: 717,001,657?\n\nWait, let me write it as a number:\n\nStarting from the hundred millions digit:\n\n1 (hundred millions) → 927,442,492\n\n8 (ten millions) → 95,267,943 → total so far 383,285,147\n\n9 (millions) →8,311,116 → total 