rite down 7 and carry over 2 to the next higher place.\n\nPosition 6 (Hundred millions): 4 (from first) + 9 (from second) + the carried over 6 = 1+5+8=2. Write 5.\n\nWait, but let me check again. Wait, the positions might be getting mixed up. Let me confirm each digit's place properly.\n\nWait, actually, when writing numbers, the first number is 749,956,624. Let's parse it:\n\nBreaking down 192,089,469:\n\n- The digits are: 7 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nSimilarly, 066,010,228:\n\n- 6 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nSo aligning them:\n\nHundred millions: 6 vs 7\n\nTen millions: 0 vs 9\n\nMillions: 5 vs1\n\nHundred thousands:0 vs1\n\nTen thousands:5 vs1\n\nThousands:9 vs9\n\nHundreds:2 vs5\n\nTens:4 vs6\n\nOnes:7 vs5\n\nWait, perhaps writing them vertically:\n\nLet me write each digit in columns:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nOnes: 4 (first) + 4 (second) = 1. No carryover. So first digit is 5.\n\nTens: 4 + 6 = 9. Second digit from right is 1.\n\nHundreds: 0 +4 =3. Third digit.\n\nThousands:8 +9=0. Fourth digit.\n\nTen thousands:4 +3=9. Fifth digit.\n\nHundred thousands:4 +5=3. Sixth digit.\n\nMillions:2 (from first number's millions place?) Wait, hold on, let's check:\n\nWait, the first number's millions place is the 9 in 699, so the millions digit is 4 (since 468 million). The second number's millions place is 2 (from 923 million). So millions place digits are 1 +5 =52? Wait, wait, maybe I messed up the positions.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to break down each number digit by digit from the right:\n\nFirst number: 008,927,373\n\nLet's write it as:\n\nDigits (from right, starting at position 0):\n\nPosition 5 (Ones): 5\n\nPosition 1 (Tens): 2\n\nPosition 9 (Hundreds):8\n\nPosition 5 (Thousands):5\n\nPosition 3 (Ten thousands):8\n\