n\nHundreds (position 7): 3 + 0 = 54. Write down 6, carryover 2.\n\nThousands (position7): 0 +8 =09 + 9 (carryover) =78. Write 4, carryover 8.\n\nTen thousands (position7): 6 +1 =7 +2=9. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands (position5):3 +4 =09. Write 3, carryover9.\n\nMillions (position1):1 +4=69 +5=79. Write 2, carryover2.\n\nTen millions (position2):1 +5=34 +7=28. Write 0, carryover5.\n\nHundred millions (position0):6 +7=5 +3=0. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nSo putting it all together, the digits from right to left would be:\n\n3 (ones),8,1,7,1,8,5,2,8. Wait, but we have to reverse that since the digits are from right to left. Wait, maybe I need to think of the result as:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\n9 (position6), 2 (position0), 2 (position5), 5 (position7), 0 (position4), 1 (position4), 4 (position6), 4 (position1), 6 (position2).\n\nSo the number is 6 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands),0 (hundreds),9 (tens),4 (ones). Wait, that doesn't seem right. Let me reconstruct the number properly.\n\nWait, the positions are:\n\nThe first digit (rightmost) is ones (9), next tens (1), hundreds (2), thousands (0), ten thousands (6), hundred thousands (0), millions (1), ten millions (7), hundred millions (0). \n\nSo writing it out from left to right (hundred millions to ones):\n\n0 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 6 (ones). \n\nTherefore the total is 720,248,701.\n\nWait, let me check that again because I might have made an error in the digit positions. Let me add the numbers step by step with another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, adding 919,973,876 + 520,613,041.\n\nLet me add them by breaking into parts:\n\n370,239,541 + 796,157,231 \n\nFirst, add the millions:\n\n258,318,154 + 315,718,614 = 077,627,151\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n493,303 + 231,702 = ?\n\n540,848 + 648,8