1)\n\nDigit 2: Millions (2)\n\nDigit 3: Hundred thousands (8)\n\nDigit 2: Ten thousands (1)\n\nDigit 4: Thousands (2)\n\nDigit 4: Hundreds (9)\n\nDigit 5: Tens (3)\n\nDigit 1: Ones (3)\n\nSecond number (800,230,757):\n\nDigit 7: Hundred millions (1)\n\nDigit 8: Ten millions (0)\n\nDigit 1: Millions (5)\n\nDigit 0: Hundred thousands (8)\n\nDigit 4: Ten thousands (3)\n\nDigit 2: Thousands (4)\n\nDigit 4: Hundreds (3)\n\nDigit 2: Tens (6)\n\nDigit 3: Ones (1)\n\nSo when adding, let's go digit by digit from right (ones) to left (hundred millions):\n\nPosition 0 (Ones): 8 +8 =74 → 7, carryover 8.\n\nPosition3 (Tens): 9 +2 =76 +4=93 → 6, carryover6.\n\nPosition5 (Hundreds):4 +2 =2 +2=4 →4, no carryover.\n\nPosition2 (Thousands):6 (from first) +6 (from second)=1 →3.\n\nPosition1 (Ten thousands):2 (first) +2 (second)=6 →1.\n\nPosition0 (Hundred thousands):3 (first) +7 (second)=3 →2.\n\nPosition4 (Millions):7 (first) +9 (second)=6 →5.\n\nPosition9 (Ten millions):3 (first) +0 (second)=6 →4.\n\nPosition4 (Hundred millions):1 (first) +8 (second)=69 →85. Wait, so here, since it's the highest place, we can just write 71. So the total sum would be 61 in the hundred millions place plus the rest.\n\nWait, but when adding the hundred millions place (position2), 0 +0 =07. So the total sum is 3,4 followed by the other digits?\n\nWait, let's see:\n\nStarting from the right, the digits after each step are:\n\nPosition6: 8\n\nPosition2:1\n\nPosition4:6\n\nPosition0:9\n\nPosition8:0\n\nPosition0:5\n\nPosition8:1\n\nPosition3:1 (from 5+9=1?)\n\nWait, let me redo the positions properly, maybe I messed up the order.\n\nWait, perhaps I should write the numbers vertically aligned:\n\n          5 2 8 7 1 3 0 1 4\n\n        + 8 8 8 8 0 6 5 7 7\n\n        -------------------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nOnes:1 +0=06 →1, carryover5.\n\nTens:0 +2=27 +5=33 →0, carryover5.\n\nHundreds:4 +9=7 +9=4 →6, carryover6.\n\nThousands:3 (from first number's thousands place) +8 (second's tho