ndard addition again.\n\nWait perhaps I made a mistake in the digit-by-digit approach.\n\nLet me try adding again step by step:\n\nFirst number: 096,811,927\n\nSecond number:300,920,797\n\nLet me write them aligned properly:\n\n          354,251,112\n        + 113,704,324\n        ---------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 5 + 2 =3\n\nTens: 7 +8=62. Write 4, carryover4.\n\nHundreds:6+9=69 +2=38. Write2, carryover9.\n\nThousands:7+0=50 +5=32. Write9, carryover8.\n\nTen thousands:5+2=2 +9=8. Write9, carryover7.\n\nHundred thousands:9+2=6. Write6.\n\nMillions:7+6=3. Write6.\n\nTen millions:2+1=68. Write2, carryover7.\n\nHundred millions:3+4=74 +6=27. Write7, carryover5.\n\nNow, the carryover8 becomes the next digit (billions place).\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nStarting from the right, the digits are:\n\nOnes:4\n\nTens:6\n\nHundreds:9\n\nThousands:2\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nMillions:9\n\nTen millions:3\n\nHundred millions:6\n\nBillions:7\n\nSo the number is 2,826,763,768.\n\nWait so in the breakdown approach earlier, I must have made an error. Let me check that again.\n\nWait in the breakdown method, I said:\n\nFirst number is 885,783,660:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n326,468,571\n\n58,745,724\n\n3 (millions place is 5?)\n\nWait 461,996,893 is 311 million, 03 million, 824 thousand, 855 thousand, 3 thousand, 8 hundred, 17, 4.\n\nWait perhaps I need to break it down properly:\n\n924,828,910 = 937,135,342 + 43,155,856 + 537,931 + 69,694 + 5,369 + 163 +84 +5.\n\nSecond number:341,872,213 = 341,552,686 +98,791,182 +997,381 +22,532 +9,392 +534 +32 +6.\n\nAdding each part:\n\nBillions: 748M +356M =3,545,932,842.\n\nHundred millions:41M +82M =313,135,745 → total so far 6,740,368,276.\n\nTen millions: 3 (from first number's ten millions place?) Wait first number's ten millions place is 9? Let me see:\n\nWait 795,115,382:\n\nDigits breakdown (from right):\n\n7 (ones)\n\n1 (tens)\n\n6 (hundreds)\n\n0 (thousands)\n\n1 (ten thousands)\n\n8 (hundred thousands