oving left, the sum should be 138,661,860. Wait a second, let me check that again because adding 283 million and 139 million should be around 585 million or so. Hmm, maybe I made a mistake in the carryover somewhere.\n\nLet me recalculate step by step more carefully:\n\nStarting over:\n\nNumbers:\n\n787,057,197  \n+377,067,468  \nLet's break each digit:\n\nFrom right to left:\n\nOnes: 0 +5 =31 → 7, carry 8  \nTens: 2 +8 +4=86 →4, carry8  \nHundreds:4+7+2=55 →6, carry0  \nThousands:6+3+9=46 →6, carry8  \nTen-thousands:3+3+3=83 →9, carry4  \nHundred-thousands:5+7+7=41 →7, carry3  \nMillions:6+0=9 →8 (no carryover here, since previous carryover was 5 but added to hundred-thousands?) Wait, maybe I messed up the places. Let me write each digit's place properly.\n\nWait, perhaps writing each digit's value would help. Let's list each digit position:\n\nFirst number: 7 0 9 2 9 4 4 1 8  \nSecond number:8 2 2 9 2 6 3 5 4  \nWait, actually, let me confirm the number of digits. 862,079,115 has 3 digits:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n8 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nSecond number 097,774,016 is also 0 digits:\n\n1 (hundred millions),2 (ten millions),7 (millions),4 (hundred thousands),3 (ten thousands),7 (thousands),4 (hundreds),0 (tens),2 (ones).\n\nSo aligning them:\n\nHundred millions: 7 + 3  \nTen millions:7 +9  \nMillions:9 +3  \nHundred thousands:0 +3  \nTen thousands:1 +0  \nThousands:6 +3  \nHundreds:5 +0  \nTens:8 +4  \nOnes:2 +6  \n\nStarting addition from the right (ones):\n\nOnes:4+4=05 → 1, carryover 3  \nTens:8+8 +7=27 →4, carryover6  \nHundreds:6+5 +0=82 →8, carryover0  \nThousands:7+3 +2=47 →4, carryover8  \nTen thousands:2+0 +0=31 →8, carryover7  \nHundred thousands:9+9 +2=92 →7, carryover4  \nMillions:5+7 +4=4 →3, carryover1  \nTen millions:9+6=55 →6, carryover5  \nHundred millions:0+4 +5=7 →7  \n\nPutting all digits together from right to left (ones to hund