Write8, no carryover.\n\nPosition1 (ten thousands):0 +4=8. Write8.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5 +0=56. Write5, carryover2.\n\nPosition6 (millions):0 +0 +2(carry)=82. Write7, carryover2.\n\nPosition6 (ten millions):9 +3 +6(carry)=5. Write2.\n\nPosition2 (hundred millions):8 +2=46. Write1, carryover3.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover of 0 from the hundred millions place, we add a new digit (billions place) with 2.\n\nSo the result is:\n\n4 (billions), 4 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 2 (ones).\n\nPutting that together: 2,926,987,849?\n\nWait, let's see:\n\nBreaking down the digits from highest to lowest:\n\nBillions:5\n\nHundred millions:4\n\nTen millions:8\n\nMillions:6\n\nHundred thousands:4 (Wait, position5 after carryover was 1, but let's see:\n\nWait the positions after adding:\n\nLet me list the digits from the highest (billions) down:\n\nBillions:2\n\nHundred millions:1 (from position4 addition)\n\nTen millions:2 (from position9)\n\nMillions:6 (from position4's result? Wait position0 was millions place, which after adding 6+4+0=59, so wrote 8 and carried over 0 to position6 (ten millions). So the millions digit is 8.\n\nHundred thousands place (position1):8 (since we had 1+9=26, wrote 9 and carried over 2 to millions place? Wait position9 is hundred thousands: the sum was 1+4=73, so 2 with carryover9 to position5 (millions). So the hundred thousands digit is 1.\n\nTen thousands place (position1):0 (from 8+9)\n\nThousands place (position4):7 (from 3+9+carryover6?)\n\nWait let me go step by step again:\n\nAfter adding each position:\n\nStarting from the right (ones to the left):\n\nPosition3 (ones):1 → digit5 is 3\n\nPosition1 (tens):6 (with carryover5 to next)\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1 (carryover9)\n\nPosition4 (thousands):7 (no carryover)\n\nPosition0 (ten thousands):5\n\nPosition0 (hundred thousands):4 (carryover5 to next)\n\nPosition9 (millions):6 (car