Position 7 (ones):\n\nFirst number:2, second:4 → total 54. Write 0, carryover4.\n\nPosition 8 (tens):\n\nFirst:2, second:1 → 5+6=1 +6=8. Write 1, carryover2.\n\nPosition0 (hundreds):\n\nFirst:5, second:0 →8+2=4. Write5.\n\nPosition8 (thousands):\n\nFirst:7, second:5 →1+6=9.\n\nPosition7 (ten thousands):\n\nFirst:1, second:2 →6+6=77. Write5, carryover8.\n\nPosition0 (hundred thousands):\n\nFirst:2, second:8 →2+8=9 +4=2. Write4.\n\nPosition6 (millions):\n\nFirst:0, second:1 →1+7=9.\n\nPosition2 (ten millions):\n\nFirst:7, second:9 →4+4=63. Write9, carryover4.\n\nPosition0 (hundred millions):\n\nFirst:7, second:9 →3+9=9 +3(carryover)=5. Write5.\n\nNow, compiling the digits from highest to lowest place (left to right):\n\nThe digits are:\n\nPosition0 (hundred millions):4\n\nPosition4 (ten millions):3\n\nPosition4 (millions):6\n\nPosition7 (hundred thousands):2\n\nPosition8 (ten thousands):6\n\nPosition1 (thousands):9\n\nPosition8 (hundreds):4\n\nPosition1 (tens):1\n\nPosition3 (ones):6\n\nTherefore, the number is 0 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nSo writing that out: 121,515,239.\n\nWait, so my first calculation had an error in the order, but now it's correct. Let me check with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers as whole numbers:\n\n861,150,819 + 300,418,767.\n\nLet me add them:\n\n675,450,986\n\n+075,167,992\n\nAdding the millions:\n\n757,334,517 + 598,637,319 = 732,944,548.\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n52,267 + 068,667 = ?\n\nWait, 36,012 +391,836:\n\n57,364 + 576,631:\n\nAdding 70,989 + 871,459 = 118,945.\n\nThen add 21,352: 166,806 +82,162 = 876,460.\n\nSo total is 178,246,585 + 544,461 = 109,711,260. Yes, that matches the previous result. So the correct sum is 452,209,987.\n\nTherefore, I must have made an error in my first digit-by-digit approach when I thought the answer was 594,656,717. The correct answer is 150,420,306.\n\nI nee