1 for first number. So 3+2=36, so yes.\n\nHundred thousands place:3 (from first number) +5 (from second number's hundred thousands place) + carryover 9. Wait, let me check:\n\nWait the first number's hundred thousands digit is 5 (from 847,935,419: the part after 981 is 235, so 4 in hundred thousands, 9 in ten thousands, 3 in thousands). The second number's hundred thousands place is 8 (from 654,429,218: the part after 891 is 731, so 8 in hundred thousands, 3 in ten thousands, 8 in thousands). So 5+4=5 plus the carryover 3 makes 56. So write 5 and carryover9.\n\nMillions place:0 (from first number's millions place) +1 (second's millions place) + carryover0. Wait first number's millions digit is 8 (the third digit from the left in 811,739,260), and second's is 3 (third digit in 721,538,082). So 8+1=39 plus 4 is 50. So write 4, carryover2.\n\nTen millions place:9 (first number's ten millions) +4 (second's ten millions) +2 (carryover) = 9. Write 5, no carryover.\n\nHundred millions place:2 +0 =2. Write 1.\n\nPutting all together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:3\n\nTens:3 (with carryover)\n\nHundreds:4\n\nThousands:2\n\nTen thousands:7 (with carryover)\n\nHundred thousands:3 (with carryover)\n\nMillions:9 (with carryover)\n\nTen millions:8\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nSo combining all digits from left to right: 4 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 7 (ones). Wait, let me check again step by step.\n\nWait the digits in each place:\n\nHundred millions:0+8=4.\n\nTen millions:3+2=4 + carryover? Wait no. Let me go step by step again, maybe I messed up in the order.\n\nWait let's do each digit step by step properly:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n2. Ones: 6 +6 =0 → 2. No carryover.\n\n9. Tens:9 +5=30 → 3, carryover 3.\n\n8. Hundreds:1 +7=75 +3=03 →0, carryover0.\n\n6. Thousands:5 +4=6 +8=3 →9, no carryover.\n\n3. Ten thousands:3 (first number) +7 (second number) =57 →8, carryover0.\n\n5. Hundred thousands:3 (first) +5 (second) =1 +3 (carryover) =98 →3, carryover8.\n\n9. Millions:1 (first) +6 (second) =96 +8 (carryover)=62 →3, carryover7.\n\n4. Ten millions:5 (first) +5 (second) =6 +2 (carryover)=1 →5, no carryover.\n\n7. Hundred millions:1 (first) +5 (second) =6 →6.\n\nSo putting all digits from highest to lowest (hundred millions to ones):\n\n4 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 4 (ones).\n\nSo the number is 905,115,745?\n\nWait, let me construct the number:\n\nHundred millions:9,\n\nTen millions:9,\n\nMillions:5,\n\nHundred thousands:4,\n\nTen thousands:0,\n\nThousands:8,\n\nHundreds:3,\n\nTens:9,\n\nOnes:5.\n\nSo combining the commas: 585,757,427.\n\nWait, let me confirm by adding another way. Let's see:\n\nFirst number:131,385,326\n\nSecond number:141,944,660\n\nAdding them:\n\n698,236,895\n\n+061,274,742\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n896,738,465 is 061 million plus 974,435.\n\n034,499,004 is 842 million plus 871,767.\n\nAdding millions:643 + 469 =319 million.\n\nAdding the remaining parts:923,310 +858,389.\n\n322,850 + 549,315:\n\n624,878 + 442,414 =828,195.\n\n83,561 +02,645 = 565,034.\n\nSo total of those parts:252,642 +655,094 =8,177,062.\n\nWait, wait that can't be right. Wait 197,551 + 441,789:\n\nLet me compute that separately.\n\n388,162\n\n+431,626\n\nAdding units:\n\nOnes:5+6=8\n\nTens:0+6=08 →0 carryover 0\n\nHundreds:4+2=65 +5=42 →2 carryover9\n\nThousands:2+3=4 +6=8\n\nTen thousands:0 +3=93 →6 carryover5\n\nHundred thousands:2 +0=1 +7=58 →7 carryover7\n\nMillions:1 (since first is 1 here, second has 7?) Wait, wait:\n\nWait 081,186 is a six-digit number: 171,461 is 2 in the hundred thousands place? Wait no, 915,499 is actually:\n\nBreaking down 353,481:\n\nHundred thousands:3 (since 423,472), ten thousands:7, thousands:6, hundreds:3, tens:7, ones:1.\n\nWait the number is 922,714. So adding to 926,987:\n\n559,