\n8 (thousands):8\n\n9 (ten thousands):7\n\n9 (hundred thousands):5\n\n5 (millions):2\n\n5 (ten millions):6\n\n1 (hundred millions):9\n\nSecond number 379,552,286:\n\nPosition 0 (ones):7\n\n3 (tens):9\n\n8 (hundreds):9\n\n3 (thousands):1\n\n2 (ten thousands):0\n\n9 (hundred thousands):1\n\n6 (millions):0\n\n9 (ten millions):8\n\n1 (hundred millions):9\n\nSo adding each position:\n\nPosition 0: 3 +2 =7 (no carryover)\n\nPosition 8: 3 +0 =62 → write 2, carryover 6\n\nPosition 4:3 +9 +7 (carry) =2 → no carryover\n\nPosition 1:3 +3 =37 → write 9, carryover 5\n\nPosition 4:0 +3 =37 + carryover 8 =40 → write 4, carryover 2\n\nPosition 1:5 +2 =74 +3=70 → write 5, carryover 8\n\nPosition 9:5 (first) +1 (second) =48 +9=39 → write 2, carryover 2\n\nPosition 2:0 (first) +5 (second) =1 +3 (carryover) =3 → no carryover\n\nPosition 2:0 (first) +0 (second) =0\n\nPutting all together from position 3 to 6 (right to left):\n\nPosition 5:0\n\nPosition 4:6\n\nPosition5:5\n\nPosition2:2\n\nPosition2:8\n\nPosition7:5\n\nPosition4:3\n\nPosition1:6\n\nPosition0:3\n\nSo the number is 082,493,290?\n\nWait, let me arrange the digits properly. The positions from right (ones) to left (hundred millions):\n\nDigits:\n\nPosition 0 (ones):8\n\nPosition 4 (tens):8\n\nPosition 5 (hundreds):4\n\nPosition9 (thousands):6\n\nPosition3 (ten thousands):9\n\nPosition8 (hundred thousands):9\n\nPosition4 (millions):8\n\nPosition2 (ten millions):9\n\nPosition0 (hundred millions):2\n\nSo the number is:\n\nHundred millions:3,\n\nTen millions:7,\n\nMillions:6,\n\nHundred thousands:6,\n\nTen thousands:5,\n\nThousands:3,\n\nHundreds:0,\n\nTens:0,\n\nOnes:2 → So combining: 991,455,465?\n\nWait, let's write it as 0 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions),1 (millions) → 988 million,\n\nThen 286 thousand... Wait, maybe better to write all digits:\n\n0 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 3 (millions),\n\n8 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands),\n\n3 (hundreds),9 (tens),0 (ones).\n\nSo 544,260,000. Let me 