hundreds), 8 (tens), 0 (ones).  \n\nNumber 2: 118,468,573  \nBreakdown:  \n- Hundred millions: 1  \n- Ten millions: 1  \n- Millions: 8  \n- Hundred thousands: 4  \n- Ten thousands: 6  \n- Thousands: 8  \n- Hundreds: 5  \n- Tens: 7  \n- Ones: 3  \n\nAdding digit by digit:  \n\nOnes: 0 + 3 = 3  \nTens: 8 +7=15 (5, carry 1)  \nHundreds: 0 +5 +1=6  \nThousands:6 +8=14 (4, carry1)  \nTen thousands:5 +6 +1=12 (2, carry1)  \nHundred thousands:6 +4 +1=11 (1, carry1)  \nMillions:6 (from first number's millions digit) + 8 (second's millions digit) +1=15 (5, carry1)  \nTen millions:3 (first's ten millions) +1 (second's ten millions) +1 (carry)=5  \nHundred millions:6 +1=7  \n\nWait, so the millions place calculation was wrong before. Let's re-calculate:\n\nMillions place: first number's millions digit is 6, second's is 8. Adding those gives 6+8=14. Then plus the carried 1 makes 15. So write down 5, carry over 1. \n\nTen millions place: first's ten millions digit is 3, second's ten millions digit is1. Adding 3+1+1 (carryover)=5. \n\nHundred millions:6+1=7. \n\nSo the digits are:\n\n- Hundred millions:7  \n- Ten millions:5  \n- Millions:5  \n- Hundred thousands:1  \n- Ten thousands:2  \n- Thousands:4  \n- Hundreds:6  \n- Tens:5  \n- Ones:3  \n\nThus the number is 755,124,653. Which matches the initial calculation. So the correct final answer is \\boxed{755124653}.\n\nWait, but when I re-examined the millions place, it's actually 6 (first number) +8 (second) +1 (carry)=15, so millions digit is 5, carryover 1 to ten millions place. Which was accounted for. \n\nYes, so the final answer is correct.  \n\n**Final Answer**  \nThe final computed sum is \\boxed{755124653}.", '']
