left:\n\nPositions 8-1:\n\nPositions 8-8: 8,9,3\n\nPosition 0:7\n\nPosition9:4\n\nPosition1:1\n\nPosition5:5\n\nPosition5:9\n\nPosition4:3\n\nSo the sum is 878,899,440?\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nWait the digits would be:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nPositions:\n\n2:1\n\n0:6\n\n4:4\n\n8:8\n\n0:9\n\n1:6\n\n5:5\n\n0:8 (since position5 had 95, so write 1 carryover 0)\n\nPosition1:3+4+9=9?\n\nWait, let me reconstruct the number:\n\nThe digits from right (position8) to left (position8):\n\nPositions:\n\n0:4\n\n6:6\n\n1:2\n\n1:5\n\n0:4\n\n4:0\n\n5:1\n\n4:5\n\n1:3\n\nSo the number is 2 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 4 (ones). Wait, that would be 945,589,185? Hmm, maybe I need to write it properly.\n\nWait, let's see:\n\nPosition4 (hundred millions): 7\n\nPosition1 (ten millions): 5\n\nPosition8 (millions):9\n\nPosition2 (hundred thousands):5\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):1\n\nPosition1 (thousands):3\n\nPosition7 (hundreds):4\n\nPosition4 (tens):6\n\nPosition2 (ones):8\n\nSo the number is 863,881,055?\n\nWait, but adding 336,298,055 and 923,756,659, let me do this another way for verification.\n\n635,826,582 + 344,781,563.\n\nAdding the millions:\n\n219,462,702 is 612 million plus 861,862.\n\n942,481,724 is 483 million plus 566,068.\n\nAdding the millions parts: 887 + 449 = 030 million.\n\nThen adding the remaining parts: 411,909 + 025,849.\n\n595,906 + 670,788:\n\n102,685 + 719,412 = 4,344,951\n\n962 + 081 = 467\n\nTotal: 0,759,025\n\nSo total sum is 522,595,239 + 0,380,761 = 221,335,605.\n\nAh, so that's correct. So the answer should be 189,363,062.\n\nBut in my first calculation, when I broke it down digit by digit, I had the same digits as that. So the previous step-by-step reasoning had an error in the millions place?\n\nWait, let me check the digit positions again carefully.\n\nWait, in the step-by-step:\n\nPosition3 (millions place):\n\nFirst number's millions 