lace:** The digits here are 5 and 7. Adding them plus the carry: 5 + 8 + 7 = 89. So, write 5 and carry over 7. But since there are no more digits left, that 4 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting all together, starting from the right, the digits are 5, 5, 9, 1, 7, 7, 7, 9, 7 with the final carried-over 4 at the front. So that would be 3,9,0,6,5,8,3,1,5,0. Wait, maybe I messed up the order here. Let me recount the places properly.\n\nWait, actually, when adding, each step corresponds to a specific place. Let me list each step's result again properly:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n- Ones: 1\n- Tens: 9 (carry 0)\n- Hundreds: 1 (carry 4)\n- Thousands: 3\n- Ten-thousands: 5 (carry 7)\n- Hundred-thousands: 3 (carry 2)\n- Millions: 6\n- Ten-millions: 7 (carry 3)\n- Hundred-millions: 0 (carry 0)\n- Then the carryover 7 becomes the next digit (billions place).\n\nSo combining all digits from right to left:\n\nBillions place: 7\n\nThen hundred-millions: 8\n\nTen-millions: 5\n\nMillions: 7\n\nHundred-thousands: 4\n\nTen-thousands: 4\n\nThousands: 6\n\nHundreds: 0\n\nTens: 1\n\nOnes: 3\n\nWait, that would be 3,143,791,830? Hmm, let me check the addition again step by step to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should write it out vertically again:\n\nLet me write each number with commas to see the places better:\n\nFirst number: 728,784,517 (which is 8 hundred fifty-one million, nine hundred seventy-five thousand, four hundred fifty-eight)\n\nSecond number: 290,541,025 (nine hundred eighty-two million, one hundred thirty-two thousand, seven hundred fifty)\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet's align the digits properly:\n\n       546,246,209\n     + 894,095,928\n     ----------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n\nOnes: 5 + 9 = 5\n\nTens: 3 + 3 = 25 → write 4, carry 8\n\nHundreds: 2 + 0 = 70, plus 5 → 06 → write 3, carry 6\n\nThousands: 7 + 6 = 0 + 4 (carry) → 0, no carry\n\nWait, thousands place digits: first number's thousands digit is 0 (since 340,481,160 is broken down as 8 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 6 (ones). Wait, maybe I miscounted the places.\n\nWait, let's break down each number digit by digit:\n\nFirst number: 1 2 3 0 6 2 8 6 5 (since it's 2 digits: 9 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 6 5 0 2 2 0 5 8 1 (7 digits: 7 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nSo when adding:\n\nLet me list each digit position:\n\nPosition 3 (ones): 5 + 4 = 7\n\nPosition 7 (tens): 6 + 9 = 49 → 7 carry 7\n\nPosition 4 (hundreds): 2 + 2 = 02 + 3 (carry) → 87 → 4 carry 9\n\nPosition 9 (thousands): 2 + 0 = 3 +7 → 4 carry 5\n\nPosition 9 (ten thousands): 2 + 6 = 28 → 6 carry 9\n\nPosition 5 (hundred thousands): 3 + 4 = 31 +0 → 84 → 7 carry 0\n\nPosition 4 (millions): 5 + 9 = 1 +9 →7 carry 3\n\nPosition 1 (ten millions): 0 +3 =98 →7 carry0\n\nPosition 1 (hundred millions):4 +3 =28 +2 →24 →9 carry5\n\nNow, since there's a carryover of 8 after the hundred millions, that adds a new digit at the billions place: 3.\n\nSo compiling all the digits from right to left (positions 6 to 8 plus the carry):\n\nBillions place: 0\n\nHundred millions: 9\n\nTen millions: 9\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nTen thousands:8\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:7\n\nOnes:3\n\nWait, but the positions are:\n\nStarting from the first digit (billions), then hundred millions down to ones. Let me arrange the digits properly:\n\nThe result digits from highest to lowest (billions down to ones):\n\n9 (billions)\n\n9 (hundred millions)\n\n8 (ten millions)\n\n7 (millions)\n\n3 (hundred thousands)\n\n9 (ten thousands)\n\n1 (thousands)\n\n6 (hundreds)\n\n2 (tens)\n\n5 (ones)\n\nWait, but that would be 4,846,833,137? Let me see:\n\nBreaking it down:\n\nBillions: 9\n\nHundred millions: 3 → 6,839,293,732\n\nTen millions:0 → +57,893,932 → total 0,469,131,786\n\nMillions:8 → +2,683,644 → 8,763,735,451\n\nHundred thousands:5 → +277,299 → 5,969,584,139\n\nTen thousands:2 → no change\n\nThousands:0 → +5,886 → 8,868,785,257\n\nHundreds:9 → +981 → 2,011,859,636\n\nTens:1 → no change\n\nOnes:0 → +0 → 4,016,345,586.\n\nYes, that seems right. Let me confirm with another method: adding the numbers as whole.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add them using another approach to verify.\n\n024,536,941 + 433,524,049.\n\nLet me add 969,711,184 + 773,616,678.\n\nFirst, add the millions:\n\n085 million + 551 million = 6,344 million.\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n080,749 + 553,899.\n\nWait, 667,262 is part of the first number's lower digits beyond millions, and 979,518 is part of the second number's lower digits?\n\nWait, perhaps breaking it down:\n\nFirst number: 077,144,897 = 019,897,459 + 807,033\n\nSecond number: 346,964,666 = 138,977,821 + 426,116\n\nAdding the millions:\n\n305,742,419 + 747,394,721 = 2,707,179,176\n\nAdding the smaller parts:\n\n709,364 + 503,928 = ?\n\nLet's compute that:\n\n418,015 + 057,141:\n\nAdding units:\n\n1 +5 =9\n\n82 +76=016 → 1 with carryover 7\n\n543 + 038 =2,762 +6 (carry)=6,085 → 7, carryover 60? Wait maybe step by step:\n\nWait 884,193:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n8 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nAdding to 841,394:\n\n9 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nOnes:3+6=0\n\nTens:8+3=43 → 5 carryover 9\n\nHundreds:2+6=08 +2=99 →1 carryover6\n\nThousands:6+9=8 +7=9 →4 no carry\n\nTen thousands:9+4=38 →2 carryover7\n\nHundred thousands:1+4=35 +3=06 →6 carryover3.\n\nSo the sum here would be 3,533,564.\n\nWait:\n\nHundred thousands place: 5 +5 =33 plus the carryover 2 makes 40 → so that's 4 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 3 to the millions.\n\nWait, so the total of 247,575 +068,628 is 7,893,022.\n\nTherefore, total sum is 2,658,545,355 + 7,821,012 = 3,399,457,170. Which matches the previous result. So that seems correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 5,770,630,361.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 251975458 and 982132750?  .\n# Reasoning:  .\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.  .\n1. The ones place: 8 + 0 = 8  .\n2. The tens place: 5 + 5 = 10 (write 0, carry over 1)  .\n3. The hundreds place: 4 + 7 + 1 = 12 (write 2, carry over 1)  .\n4. The thousands place: 5 + 2 + 1 = 8  .\n5. The ten-thousands place: 7 + 3 = 10 (write 0, carry over 1)  .\n6. The hundred-thousands place: 9 + 1 + 1 = 11 (write 1, carry over 1)  .\n7. The millions place: 1 + 2 + 1 = 4  .\n8. The ten-millions place: 5 + 8 = 13 (write 3, carry over 1)  .\n9. The hundred-millions place: 2 + 9 + 1 = 12 (write 2, carry over 1)  .\n10. The billions place: 1 (from the final carry-over)  .\n\nAnswer:. Therefore, the answer is"]] 65%|######4   | 323/500 [2:57:19<1:29:34, 30.36s/it]
