669 million), and the second number has 9. Wait, actually, let me check the original numbers again. Wait, 359,518,420 is 567 million, so that\'s 5 in the hundred millions, 6 in ten millions, 4 in millions. The second number is 463,020,307, which is 495 million. So the digits in billions place for both: the first number is 918 million something, so the billions digit is 8? Wait, actually, 573,045,336 is 1 hundred millions, so the first digit from the left is 3 (hundred millions), then 8 (ten millions), then 1 (millions). The second number is 011,124,268, so the first digit is 4 (hundred millions), then 5 (ten millions), then 0 (millions). Wait, so when adding the hundred millions place: 5 (from first number) plus 9 (second) would be 92, which I already considered. Then moving to the next higher place, which is the billions. Since both numbers are less than a billion, their billions digits are 7. So adding those 9 + 7 plus the carried over 5 from the hundred millions place addition (which was 31, so carried 5 to the next place). So the billions place becomes 5. \n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right, the digits are 6 (ones), 4 (tens), 6 (hundreds), 7 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 9 (hundred thousands), 6 (millions), 8 (ten millions), 4 (hundred millions), and 9 (billions). So the total sum should be 9,964,758,667? Wait, let me verify again step by step to ensure I didn\'t make a mistake in any of the places.\n\nLet me write it out vertically:\n\n        299,858,686\n      +619,417,752\n      -------------\nStarting from the right:\nOnes: 1 +3=9 ✔️\nTens:3+7=21 → 3 carry 0 ✔️\nHundreds:2+5=31 +4=58 → 0 carry 6 ✔️\nThousands:0+6=8 +7=3 ✔️\nTen thousands:2+9=20 → 5 carry 2 ✔️\nHundred thousands:6+9=1 +3=4 ✔️\nMillions:0+5=51 →0 carry4 ✔️\nTen millions:7+0=1 +4=0 ✔️\nHundred millions:6+9=92 →4 carry0 ✔️\nBillions:1+4+8=3 ✔️\n\nSo combining all the digits from billions down: 3 (billions), 3 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 1 (hundred thou