dred millions place: first number has an 7, second has a 8. 9 + 7 = 2, plus the carried 7 makes 85. So we write 8 here and carry over 5.\n\nFinally, the billions place. The first number has an 0, and the second has nothing (since it's a 1-digit number). Adding the carried 9 gives 0 + 7 +4 = 3. Wait, actually, the first number is 429,874,233 which is 6 digits, so the highest place is the hundred millions. Wait, maybe I messed up the digit places earlier. Let me check again.\n\nWait, let me recount the digits. Let's write both numbers with commas to see their places clearly:\n\nFirst number: 307,471,532. Breaking it down:\n- 1 (hundred millions)\n- 5 (ten millions)\n- 7 (millions)\n- 8 (hundred thousands)\n- 3 (ten thousands)\n- 6 (thousands)\n- 8 (hundreds)\n- 3 (tens)\n- 9 (ones)\n\nSecond number: 417,495,230. Breaking down:\n- 0 (hundred millions)\n- 1 (ten millions)\n- 1 (millions)\n- 8 (hundred thousands)\n- 6 (ten thousands)\n- 4 (thousands)\n- 5 (hundreds)\n- 1 (tens)\n- 0 (ones)\n\nWait, so when adding, the hundred millions place would be 3 + 4 = 5, but earlier when I added ten millions place, I had 9 +5? Wait, let me redo the addition step by step properly.\n\nLet me align them properly:\n\n        912,731,699\n      + 616,584,749\n      ----------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 9 + 7 = 7. Write 0.\n\nTens: 5 + 8 = 3. Write 9.\n\nHundreds: 9 + 4 = 2. Write 7.\n\nThousands: 8 + 6 = 79. Write 6, carryover 7.\n\nTen thousands: 9 + 4 =91 + 5 (carry) =23. Write 9, carryover 2.\n\nHundred thousands: 5 + 0 =34 +8 =02. Write 5, carryover 6.\n\nMillions: 0 + 4 =56 +0 =78. Write 4, carryover 4.\n\nTen millions: 8 +8 =52 +7 =33. Write 1, carryover 5.\n\nHundred millions: 7 +7 =4 +4 (carry) =61. Wait, here, the hundred millions digits are 2 and 7. So 2 +0 =8, plus the carryover 5 makes 08. So we write 6 in the hundred millions place and carryover 8 to the next higher place (billions).\n\nBut the original numbers don't have a billions digit except the first number's 4 is in hundred millions. So the billions place would get that carried 3. So the final digit is 6 in the billions place followed by the 5 in hundred millions. \n\nSo putting it all together, the sum would be 2,161,598,254?\n\nWait, let me check that again step by step:\n\nLet me do the addition step by step digit by digit with positions:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nPosition 0 (ones): 0 +7 =9 → 1\n\nPosition 8 (tens):9 +9 =2 →1\n\nPosition1 (hundreds):8 +3=5 →2\n\nPosition1 (thousands):6 +5=67 → write 9, carryover 5\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):8 +2=99 +6=95 →0, carryover9\n\nPosition4 (hundred thousands):1 +8=58 +4=68 →5, carryover7\n\nPosition1 (millions):1 +8=58 +7=60 →7, carryover7\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):3 +9=94 +4=63 →6, carryover4\n\nPosition3 (hundred millions):3 +9=3 +7=67 →7, carryover8\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carryover9 becomes a new digit at the billions place. So the final number is 2 followed by the digits we have. So the total is 5,343,456,400?\n\nWait, let me verify using another method. Let me add the numbers as whole numbers:\n\n243,204,001 + 011,841,379.\n\nAdding them:\n\nFirst number: 667,771,046\n\nSecond number: 971,741,188\n\nAdding:\n\nLet me add the millions first. 936 million +099 million = 3,793 million.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 657 thousand 904 + 587 thousand 194.\n\n731,574 + 707,030.\n\nAdding those:\n\n349,774 + 456,130:\n\nAdding thousands: 385,533 + 295,384 = 6,418,111.\n\nThen the rest: 051 + 583 = 323.\n\nSo total of those two parts is 7,426,431 + 427 = 4,099,810.\n\nNow adding to the millions total:\n\n5,185,316,845 + 6,539,453 = 5,837,193,146.\n\nOkay, that matches. So the final answer should be 8,467,937,237. Let me check the digits again step by step to make sure I didn't make any mistake in the initial digit-wise addition.\n\nBreaking down each digit:\n\nLet me write both numbers with all digits separated:\n\nFirst number: 6 1 7 5 9 0 8 0 8\n\nSecond number:2 7 9 9 9 6 0 2 6\n\nWait, actually, let me list them digit by digit from right to left (since addition starts from the right):\n\nFirst number (106,609,124):\n\nPositions (from right, starting at 0):\n\n4:5 (ones)\n\n7:4 (tens)\n\n9:9 (hundreds)\n\n5:7 (thousands)\n\n7:0 (ten thousands)\n\n3:1 (hundred thousands)\n\n9:5 (millions)\n\n2:5 (ten millions)\n\n1:3 (hundred millions)\n\nSecond number (086,225,809):\n\nPositions:\n\n9:5 (ones)\n\n6:7 (tens)\n\n7:3 (hundreds)\n\n9:4 (thousands)\n\n4:2 (ten thousands)\n\n9:1 (hundred thousands)\n\n8:5 (millions)\n\n2:5 (ten millions)\n\n6:7 (hundred millions)\n\nNow adding each position:\n\nPosition 7:0+8=3\n\nPosition4:3+2=2\n\nPosition7:9+2=3\n\nPosition1:6+8=38 → 7, carry 8\n\nPosition1:2+4=74 +3=79 →5, carry5\n\nPosition7:8+6=04 +3=65 →4, carry8\n\nPosition1:4+5=72 +2=36 →7, carry8\n\nPosition9:2+7=88 +6=64 →8, carry4\n\nPosition1:2+5=0 +2=72 →9, carry8\n\nThen the carryover0 becomes the next digit (position37):3.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\n3 (position6),4,6,0 (with carry),6,6,7,1,7, and the final 7.\n\nSo written left to right, it's 6 (billion), 8 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 5 (hundreds),8 (tens),6 (ones). Wait, no. Wait, the digits are:\n\nThe final digits after each step from position2 to position07 (including the carry):\n\nPosition46:7\n\nPosition3:3\n\nPosition5:1\n\nPosition4:6\n\nPosition1:8\n\nPosition9:1\n\nPosition9:8 (but wait, let me see):\n\nWait, when listing the digits from the highest position first:\n\nThe final number has 45 digits: 3 (billions place), then the rest.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nBillions:6\n\nHundred millions:6\n\nTen millions:8\n\nMillions:5\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:8 (from position8 which was 74 leading to a 6 in thousands place, but wait, let me track again.\n\nWait perhaps I need to list each digit properly.\n\nAfter adding each position:\n\nStarting from position0 (ones) up to