thousands)\n- 7 (ten thousands)\n- 8 (thousands)\n- 0 (hundreds)\n- 3 (tens)\n- 3 (ones)\n\nWait, so the millions place for the first number is 3, and the second is 0. So adding them with the carryover: 6+4 +9 (carryover) = 4. So that's correct.\n\nNext, the ten millions place: the first number has 0 and the second has 8. So 6 + 6 = 0. But wait, do I have any carryover here? Wait, the previous step was the millions place, which had a carryover, but the ten millions place here doesn't have any carryover from the millions step because the millions addition was 0+2+9=5, which doesn't exceed 48. So ten millions is 1 +2 =5.\n\nThen the hundred millions place: 6 and 2. 5 +4=4. \n\nWait, but let me go step by step again to make sure. Maybe I missed a digit. Let me write each digit's place:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 6 + 8 =7\n\nTens: 0 +7 =6\n\nHundreds: 2 +3 =1\n\nThousands: 7 +0=6\n\nTen-thousands:8 (from first) +4 (second) =0\n\nHundred-thousands:7 +9 =88 → write 4, carryover 9\n\nMillions:5 (first) +0 (second) +9 (carryover) =4\n\nTen millions:3 (first) +4 (second)=0\n\nHundred millions:8 +9=4\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nThe digits from right to left (ones to hundred millions) would be:\n\n0 (ones),6 (tens),1 (hundreds),5 (thousands),6 (ten-thousands),5 (hundred thousands),6 (millions),9 (ten millions),0 (hundred millions).\n\nSo writing the number from left to right, it's 748,853,533?\n\nWait, let me check that again. Wait, the digits are arranged as:\n\nHundred millions:9\n\nTen millions:3\n\nMillions:6\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:6\n\nThousands:0\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:1\n\nOnes:3\n\nSo combining them: 9 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 0 (ones). So the number is 908,650,563?\n\nWait a second, maybe I made a mistake in the place values. Let me reconstruct the number step by step:\n\nStarting from the highest place:\n\nHundred millions place:0 →