arry 3\n\nPosition1:5 +2 =2 →5\n\nPosition0:5 (from first) +4 (second)=3 →7\n\nPosition9:4 (first) +0 (second)=32 →3, carryover2\n\nPosition8:9 (first) +3 (second)=2 +9 (carryover)=9 →5\n\nSo putting all together from Position5 to Position5:\n\nThe digits are:\n\nPosition3:9\n\nPosition1:5\n\nPosition5:3\n\nPosition1:6\n\nPosition6:1\n\nPosition5:1\n\nPosition9:4\n\nPosition9:7\n\nPosition7:4\n\nSo the number is 7 (hundred millions),4 (ten millions),5 (millions),3 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),1 (thousands),9 (hundreds),3 (tens),3 (units). Wait, let me arrange them properly.\n\nWait, the positions from left to right would be:\n\nPosition2 (hundred millions):6\n\nPosition1 (ten millions):0\n\nPosition4 (millions):0\n\nPosition2 (hundred thousands):3\n\nPosition7 (ten thousands):0\n\nPosition8 (thousands):3\n\nPosition2 (hundreds):0\n\nPosition7 (tens):0\n\nPosition2 (units):7\n\nSo combining all digits: 0 7 0 2 0 1 0 1 0 → 742,208,811?\n\nWait, let me check that again. Wait, maybe I miscounted the digits. Let's see:\n\nThe digits from highest to lowest (left to right):\n\nPosition0: 1 (hundred millions place)\n\nPosition3:6 (ten millions)\n\nPosition6:8 (millions)\n\nPosition2:6 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition7:4 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition2:9 (thousands)\n\nPosition5:2 (hundreds)\n\nPosition4:0 (tens)\n\nPosition2:7 (units)\n\nSo the number is 913,157,200.\n\nWait, let me verify with another method. Let me add the two numbers:\n\n116,396,871\n\n+309,932,772\n\nAdding them step by step:\n\nFirst, add the millions:\n\n154,942,296 is 174 million plus 759,310.\n\n939,781,432 is 366 million plus 82,742.\n\nAdding the millions: 105 + 780 = 577 million.\n\nThen add the remaining parts: 059,297 + 43,636.\n\n919,315 + 05,314 = 311,782; then +2,897 = 049,966.\n\nSo total is 507,859,659 + 650,778 = 580,769,588. That matches the previous result. So the answer should be 536,173,528. Let me check if the digit-wise addition was correct.\n\nWait, in the digit-by-digit break