t by digit (from right to left):\n\nPosition 9 (ones): 2\n\nPosition 5 (tens): 5\n\nPosition 4 (hundreds): 4\n\nPosition 2 (thousands): 7\n\nPosition 4 (ten thousands): 8\n\nPosition 7 (hundred thousands): 1\n\nPosition 3 (millions): 4\n\nPosition 3 (ten millions): 8\n\nPosition 5 (hundred millions): 7\n\nWait, actually, let me count the digits properly. Let's see:\n\nThe first number is 812,807,044. Let's count the digits without commas:\n\n4 3 1 9 2 3 9 5 0. So that's 3 digits. So the places are:\n\nBillions (position 4): 4\n\nHundred millions (7): 7\n\nTen millions (0): 7\n\nMillions (8):2\n\nHundred thousands (7):7\n\nTen thousands (6):7\n\nThousands (1):9\n\nHundreds (8):4\n\nTens (8):0\n\nWait, maybe I mixed up the order here. Let's clarify:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place as position 5):\n\nPosition 8: 5 (ones)\n\nPosition 4: 3 (tens)\n\nPosition 6: 2 (hundreds)\n\nPosition 6: 8 (thousands)\n\nPosition 1: 7 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition 3:1 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition 1:4 (millions)\n\nPosition 1:9 (ten millions)\n\nPosition 4:7 (hundred millions)\n\nSimilarly, the second number is 231,485,224.\n\nBreaking it down digit by digit (without commas):\n\n4 7 7 2 0 8 6 9 2.\n\nWait, that's 8 digits as well. Let me list them from right to left (positions 7 to 8):\n\nPosition 8:5 (ones)\n\nPosition 7:3 (tens)\n\nPosition 2:6 (hundreds)\n\nPosition 7:7 (thousands)\n\nPosition 8:0 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition 5:2 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition 6:7 (millions)\n\nPosition 9:3 (ten millions)\n\nPosition 3:0 (hundred millions)\n\nWait, let me confirm that again. Let's write the second number as 854,426,888:\n\nBreaking down with commas:\n\n7 (hundred millions), 51 (ten millions and millions?), Wait, commas are placed every three digits. So 118,083,054 is:\n\n5 (hundred millions), 91 (ten millions and millions?), actually:\n\n1 1 4 , 0 5 6 , 4 9 1\n\nSo the digits from left to right are:\n\n5 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands)