ct addition is 332,185. So my earlier method had an error in the ten thousands place's carryover?\n\nHmm, okay, so maybe my initial digit-by-digit approach had an error. Let me check again.\n\nWait, in the hundreds place: 5 (from 07,965) +9 (from 38,439) =09 → write 9, carryover8 to thousands.\n\nThousands place:7 (from first) +7 (second) =66 +8=01 → write6, carryover7 to ten thousands.\n\nTen thousands place:5 +8 =51 +8 (carryover) =60 → write9, carryover6 to hundred thousands.\n\nSo the hundred thousands place has that 5. So the number is 7 (hundred thousands) 3 (ten thousands) 1 (thousands) 5 (hundreds) 0 (tens) 4 (ones). So 874,511. That matches the numerical calculation. So my previous mistake was in thinking the ten thousands place would have 52 leading to 6 in the ten thousands and carryover, but the hundred thousands gets the carryover, making it 429,942.\n\nOkay, so going back to the original problem. The total of the two numbers is 8,754,258,964 (from the millions part) plus 424,653 (from the remaining parts). So total is 5,983,454,311?\n\nWait, no. Wait the millions parts: 883 million +718 million = 9,281 million. Then the remaining parts: 803,982 +379,910 = 0,959,521? Wait wait, no. Wait I think I messed up the breakdown.\n\nWait original numbers:\n\nFirst number:599,407,456 is 807,165,729 + 865,055.\n\nSecond number:537,385,910 is 542,921,654 +151,353.\n\nAdding the millions parts:061,438,199 +675,498,833 = 7,256,281,449.\n\nAdding the remaining parts:186,613 +553,331.\n\nEarlier, I computed that as 6,931,881? Wait, no, when I added 601,634 +493,689, I think I miscalculated.\n\nWait 132,177 +789,126:\n\nLet me do that again:\n\n852,570\n\n+559,368\n\n--------\n\nAdding:\n\nUnits place:8+3=5\n\nTens:2+4=5\n\nHundreds:7+1=97 →8, carryover8.\n\nThousands:5+1=88 +7=89 →7, carryover3.\n\nTen thousands:1 (from 167,612's ten thousands place? Wait 060,563 is 6 (hundred thousands),3 (ten thousands),7 (thousands). Wait no:\n\nWait 327,049 is:\n\n4 (hundred thousa