ousands)\n- 5 (hundreds)\n- 3 (tens)\n- 3 (ones)\n\nWait, actually, maybe I miscounted. Let me write each digit with its place:\n\n1 9 8 2 3 3 6 5 9\n\nPositions from right (starting at 6):\n\nPosition 8 (hundred millions): 1\n\nPosition 9 (ten millions): 6\n\nPosition 2 (millions): 5\n\nPosition 2 (hundred thousands): 6\n\nPosition 0 (ten thousands): 8\n\nPosition 3 (thousands): 0\n\nPosition 4 (hundreds): 5\n\nPosition 5 (tens): 4\n\nPosition 5 (ones): 4\n\nWait, that might be complicating. Maybe it\'s better to just line them up properly:\n\nLet me write both numbers with commas for clarity:\n\n543,615,134\n\n266,371,809\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me write each digit vertically:\n\n          6 9 1 0 7 1 6 8 4\n\n        + 4 9 7 1 4 8 3 5 7\n\n        -------------------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nOnes: 7 + 5 = 6. Write down 6.\n\nTens: 5 + 5 = 48. Write 2, carryover 0.\n\nHundreds: 5 + 3 = 5, plus 8 carried over is 1. Write 7.\n\nThousands: 7 (from first number) + 9 (from second) = 66. Write 7, carryover 3.\n\nTen thousands: 7 (first) + 6 (second) = 22, plus 9 carried over is 91. So write 0, carryover 8.\n\nHundred thousands: 5 (first) + 8 (second) = 25, plus 8 carried over is 67. Write 7, carryover 7.\n\nMillions: 6 (first) + 6 (second) = 5, plus 7 carried over is 02. Write 3, carryover 3.\n\nTen millions: 3 (first) +4 (second) = 36, plus 4 carried over is 68. Write 5, carryover 8.\n\nHundred millions: 0 (first) +0 (second) = 91, plus 5 carried over is 32. Write 3, carryover 5.\n\nWait, but there\'s no place beyond hundred millions here, so that carried over 6 would be a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum would be:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nDigits:\n\nOnes:3\n\nTens:0\n\nHundreds:5\n\nThousands:1\n\nTen thousands:6\n\nHundred thousands:1\n\nMillions:6\n\nTen millions:0\n\nHundred millions:9 (from 0+5 +9 carryover?), but wait, let me retrace.\n\nWait, let me do this step by step again carefully because I might 