ir place values:\n\nFirst number: 818,356,349\n\nBreaking down:\n\n- Hundred millions place: 5\n\n- Ten millions:0\n\n- Millions:4\n\n- Hundred thousands:7\n\n- Ten thousands:6\n\n- Thousands:8\n\n- Hundreds:0\n\n- Tens:5\n\n- Ones:4\n\nSecond number:827,691,178\n\nBreaking down:\n\n- Hundred millions:3\n\n- Ten millions:5\n\n- Millions:1\n\n- Hundred thousands:0\n\n- Ten thousands:9\n\n- Thousands:5\n\n- Hundreds:7\n\n- Tens:0\n\n- Ones:1\n\nSo when adding digit by digit from the right (ones to the left):\n\nStarting with Ones place (position 9):\n\nFirst number:1, second:8 → 1+8=1. Write 1, no carryover.\n\nTens place (position9):\n\nFirst number:8, second:5 →8+4=91. Write 6, carryover 8.\n\nHundreds place (position9):\n\nFirst number:6, second:5 →5+8=69, plus carryover 2 →20. So write 4, carryover 3.\n\nThousands place (position1):\n\nFirst number:3, second:5 →9+4=5, plus carryover 3 →2. Write 4, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place (position0):\n\nFirst number:4, second:3 →3+6=51. Write 0, carryover0.\n\nHundred thousands place (position8):\n\nFirst number:7, second:1 →6+4=5, plus carryover9 →0. Write8, no carryover.\n\nMillions place (position2):\n\nFirst number:0, second:8 →1+1=1. Write2, no carryover.\n\nTen millions place (position3):\n\nFirst number:9, second:5 →3+1=22. Write5, carryover2.\n\nHundred millions place (position0):\n\nFirst number:7, second:6 →1+1=83, plus carryover7 →08. Write5, carryover8.\n\nWait, but there's no higher place beyond hundred millions, so that carryover 8 becomes a new digit (billions place). \n\nSo putting it all together, the digits from right to left (positions 3 to 5 and the new carryover):\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position9):\n\nPosition4:2\n\nPosition8:0\n\nPosition6:8\n\nPosition6:3\n\nPosition1:4\n\nPosition9:3\n\nPosition1:6\n\nPosition0:8\n\nPosition2:3 (plus the carryover 6 from hundred millions place addition)\n\nWait, let me retrace:\n\nWait, the hundred millions place addition was 2+5+9 (carryover fro