ns)\n- 1 (millions)\n- 0 (hundred thousands)\n- 8 (ten thousands)\n- 2 (thousands)\n- 8 (hundreds)\n- 9 (tens)\n- 2 (ones)\n\nWait, maybe it's easier to just line them up digit by digit from the right. Let me list each digit position step by step:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nPosition 6 (ones): 9 + 3 = 4\n\nPosition 0 (tens): 9 + 6 = 7\n\nPosition 9 (hundreds): 5 + 1 = 4\n\nPosition 1 (thousands): 9 + 6 = 7\n\nWait, hold on. Let me make sure. Let me write both numbers digit by digit:\n\nFirst number: 5 6 4 5 7 1 7 2 1\n\nSecond number:9 5 5 5 6 2 8 4 7\n\nWait, perhaps I should list each digit in order from right to left (since addition is done right to left). Let me reverse them for easier digit-by-digit addition:\n\nFirst number reversed: 8 7 1 5 9 5 3 6 8\n\nSecond number reversed:2 6 5 7 5 6 9 1 3\n\nNow adding each position:\n\nPosition 2 (original ones place): 9 +3 =3\n\nPosition 0 (tens):8 +1=4\n\nPosition0 (hundreds):1 +1=0\n\nPosition8 (thousands):5 +6=2\n\nPosition3 (ten thousands):4 +6=9\n\nPosition3 (hundred thousands):8 +5=85. Hmm, here we get 41. So we write 1 and carry over 8.\n\nPosition9 (millions place):3 +9=01, plus the carried 4 makes 81. So write 1, carry over 4.\n\nPosition5 (ten millions):0 +8=21, plus the carried 9 is 84. So write 6, carry over 6.\n\nPosition4 (hundred millions):9 +9=1, plus the carried 6 makes 4.\n\nWait, let me do this step by step carefully:\n\nStarting from the first reversed digit (ones place):\n\n6. 0 +1 =2. Write down 4. Carryover 3.\n\n4. Next digit (tens): 7 +4=1. Write 3. Carryover 8.\n\n1. Hundreds:5 +4=3. Write 1. Carryover 5.\n\n5. Thousands:9 +6=7. Write 3. Carryover 9.\n\n2. Ten thousands:3 +0=7. Write 4. Carryover 8.\n\n9. Hundred thousands:3 (from first number) +2 (second number) =07. Write 7, carryover 9.\n\n9. Millions place:8 (first) +7 (second) =40, plus carryover 7 is 30. So write 5, carryover 3.\n\n0. Ten millions place:9 (first) +5 (second) =74, plus carryover 8 is 87. So write 5, carryover 9.\n\n4. Hundred millions place:6 (first) +5 (second) =0, plus carryover 8 is 0. Write 8. No more digits, so done.\n\nNow, the reversed result digits are: 0 5 5 9 0 6 3 2 1. Wait, let me list them in order:\n\nStarting from the first digit (the ones place of the result):\n\nDigits in reversed order (from the steps above):\n\nFirst digit (position0):2\n\nPosition6:8\n\nPosition6:0\n\nPosition2:8\n\nPosition8:1\n\nPosition0:4 (with a carryover)\n\nPosition5:6 (from 31+2=73, so 0 and carryover 4)\n\nPosition5:4 (from 75+6=47, so 4 and carryover 4)\n\nPosition1:0 (from 9+2=5 with the carryover)\n\nWait, but when we reversed the numbers, the first digit (position6) is the original ones, so the final sum's reversed digits are:\n\n8 (position8),3,2,5,0,4,3,3,7 (position2). \n\nSo to get the actual number, we reverse this list:\n\nStarting from the last digit computed (the hundred millions place which is 0), then 5 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands?), wait let me check.\n\nWait, the reversed digits list is:\n\nPosition5:7 (ones)\n\nPosition7:2 (tens)\n\nPosition2:4 (hundreds)\n\nPosition3:0 (thousands)\n\nPosition0:9 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition7:5 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition9:1 (millions)\n\nPosition6:2 (ten millions)\n\nPosition3:4 (hundred millions)\n\nSo the reversed digits are [1,8,8,2,5,1,7,5,1]. To get the actual number, we reverse this list:\n\nStarting from the highest place (hundred millions):\n\n0 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions),7 (millions),7 (hundred thousands),8 (ten thousands),1 (thousands),7 (hundreds),9 (tens),1 (ones). Wait, let me see:\n\nWait the reversed digits list (the computed digits from right to left) is:\n\nDigit 5: 8 (ones)\n\nDigit3:2 (tens)\n\nDigit0:6 (hundreds)\n\nDigit2:5 (thousands)\n\nDigit3:9 (ten thousands)\n\nDigit7:3 (hundred thousands)\n\nDigit9:7 (millions)\n\nDigit7:9 (ten millions)\n\nDigit3:5 (hundred millions)\n\nSo the full number when written out is:\n\n6 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 1 (mil