er8\n\nTen millions:3 +7=6 +3=6 →0, no carryover\n\nHundred millions:4 +7=00 →4, carryover9\n\nThen the final carryover7.\n\nSo the sum is 8,342,290,979.\n\nWait, but when I did the other method, breaking into 153M +884M etc., I got 5,747,343,338. That must be an error in that method. Let me check that again.\n\nWait in the other method:\n\n433,990,764 +533,403,843\n\nI split as (766,352,875 +00,722,592) + (171,355,853 +33,365,923) = 0,955,518,733 + (02,775,868 +72,121,523)\n\nThen 97,285,637 +60,208,458:\n\n91,049,813 +13,328,028:\n\nAdding 75,661,183 +97,146,438 =18,299,763\n\nThen add the remaining 601,653:\n\n52,742,682 +811,131 = 73,847,967.\n\nWait, so total is 4,359,444,188 +18,643,537 =0,135,591,046?\n\nWait, that would be 5,182,900,976. Wait, but earlier I thought it was 2,661,553,440. So perhaps I added wrong there.\n\nWait let me recompute:\n\n83,692,212 +28,510,142:\n\n20,062,162 +63,509,884:\n\nLet me add digit by digit:\n\n73,245,938\n\n+57,870,144\n\nStarting from units:\n\n0+2=3\n\n5+8=23 →9, carryover3\n\n6+9=77 +5=83 →5, carryover6\n\n4+9=63 +7=61 →6, carryover9\n\n4+9=2 +5=4\n\n8+4=8\n\n2+0=03 →8, carryover5\n\nThe remaining digits:\n\nThe first number has 1 (millions place?), wait, perhaps better to do the addition:\n\n16,153,275 is 16,063,835\n\n+21,913,817\n\nAdding:\n\n30,894,975\n\n+92,033,346\n\n= (99,973,993 +802,174) + (96,755,172 +280,247)\n\n= (96M +84M) =62M, plus (863,508 +472,117)=6,401,117\n\nThus total 20,398,237 +8,318,528 =33,972,643.\n\nSo total sum is 7,948,252,694 +03,747,680 =4,556,392,796.\n\nWait, but the digit-by-digit method gave 8,454,548,523. Hmm, now there's a difference of 5 million here. Wait, so where is the mistake?\n\nWait 72,021,065 +84,932,698:\n\nLet me add them directly:\n\n20,519,724\n\n+12,351,481\n\nAdding units place:\n\n9+6=0\n\nTens:7+0=02 →6, carryover0\n\nHundreds:3+9=06 +8=97 →7 carryover0\n\nThousands:5+5=48 +0=43 →3 carryover8\n\nTen thousands:0+0=3 +9=3\n\nHundred thousands:6+4=00 →4 carryover8\n\nM