yover.\n\nPosition1 (tens):\n\n0 +5 =5 →5, no carryover.\n\nPosition2 (hundreds):\n\n2 +3 =5 →5, no carryover.\n\nPosition3 (thousands):\n\n7 +7 =14 →4, carryover1.\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):\n\n7 (first) +3 (second) +1 (carryover) =11 →1, carryover1.\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands):\n\n0 (first) +6 (second) +1 (carryover)=7 →7, no carryover.\n\nPosition6 (millions):\n\n1 (first) +2 (second)=3 →3, no carryover.\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):\n\n9 (first) +8 (second)=17 →7, carryover1.\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):\n\n9 (first) +5 (second) +1 (carryover)=15 →5, carryover1.\n\nNow, since we've reached the highest digit (hundred millions), the carryover1 becomes the billions place.\n\nSo the digits from position0 to position9 are:\n\nPosition9 (billions):1\n\nPosition8:5\n\nPosition7:7\n\nPosition6:3\n\nPosition5:7\n\nPosition4:1\n\nPosition3:4\n\nPosition2:5\n\nPosition1:5\n\nPosition0:3\n\nSo the total is 1,5 (billions),5 (hundred millions),7 (ten millions),3 (millions),7 (hundred thousands),1 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),5 (hundreds),5 (tens),3 (ones).\n\nWait, let's write that out:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:5\n\nTen millions:7\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:5\n\nOnes:3\n\nSo the number is 1,573,714,553?\n\nWait, let's build it step by step:\n\nStarting from billions place:1\n\nThen hundred millions:5 → 1,5\n\nTen millions:7 →15,7\n\nMillions:3 →157,3\n\nHundred thousands:7 →1,573,7\n\nTen thousands:1 →15,737,1\n\nThousands:4 →157,371,4\n\nHundreds:5 →1,573,714,5\n\nTens:5 →15,737,145\n\nOnes:3 →157,371,453\n\nWait, but with the billions digit:\n\nTotal number is 1,573,714,553?\n\nWait:\n\n1 (billions) ×1,000,000,000 =1,000,000,000\n\n5 (hundred millions) ×100,000,000 =500,000,000 → total so far 1,500,000,000\n\n7 (ten millions) ×10,000,000 =70,000,000 → 1,570,000,000\n\n3 (millions) ×1,000,000 =3,000,000 →1,573,000,000\n\n7 (hundred thousands) ×100,000 =700,000 →1,573,700,000\n\n1 (ten thou