lions and hundred millions), but in the breakdown, it's 900M+500M=1400M, which is 1.4 billion, but with the carryover, it's 1.5 billion?\n\nWait, 900 million plus 500 million is 1,400 million (which is 1.4 billion). Adding the 99 million gives 1.499 billion. So the total should be around 1.5 billion, which matches the breakdown.\n\nBut in the digit-by-digit, the total was 1,573 million? Wait, perhaps I miscounted the positions.\n\nWait let's re-express the digit-by-digit result correctly:\n\nThe digits from position9 to position0 are:\n\nPosition9 (billions):1\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):5\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):7\n\nPosition6 (millions):3\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands):7\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):1\n\nPosition3 (thousands):4\n\nPosition2 (hundreds):5\n\nPosition1 (tens):5\n\nPosition0 (ones):3\n\nSo the number is:\n\n1 (billions) →1,000,000,000\n\n+5 (hundred millions) →500,000,000 → total 1,500,000,000\n\n+7 (ten millions) →70,000,000 →1,570,000,000\n\n+3 (millions) →3,000,000 →1,573,000,000\n\n+7 (hundred thousands) →700,000 →1,573,700,000\n\n+1 (ten thousands) →10,000 →1,573,710,000\n\n+4 (thousands) →4,000 →1,573,714,000\n\n+5 (hundreds) →500 →1,573,714,500\n\n+5 (tens) →50 →1,573,714,550\n\n+3 (ones) →1,573,714,553.\n\nWait but the breakdown method gives 1,500,714,553. The difference is in the ten millions and millions places.\n\nWait why the discrepancy?\n\nAh, because in the breakdown method, when I added the 917,077,201:\n\n917,077,201 is 900,000,000 +17,000,000 +77,000 +201.\n\nThe second number:582,637,352 is 500,000,000 +82,000,000 +637,000 +352.\n\nAdding the ten millions parts:\n\n17M (from first) +82M (second) =99M → which is 99,000,000.\n\nThen the millions parts: the first number has 77,000 (hundred thousands and below) and the second has 637,000.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to re-express the breakdown:\n\nFirst number breakdown:\n\n917,077,201 = 900,000,000 + 17,000,000 + 77,000 + 201\n\nSecond number breakdown:\n\n582,637,352 = 500,000,000 + 82,000,000 + 637,000 + 352\n\nAdding:\n\n900M +500M =1,400M\n\n17M +82M =99M → total 1,499M\n\n77k +637k =714k → total 1,500,714,000\n\n201 +352 =553 → total 1,500,714,553.\n\nWait this suggests the correct total is 1,500,714,553, but the digit-by-digit gave 1,573,714,553. So there's a difference of 73,000,000.\n\nAh! The mistake must be in the digit-by-digit addition. Let's redo it carefully.\n\nFirst number: 917,077,201\n\nSecond number:582,637,352\n\nAligning digits:\n\nFirst number:9 1 7 0 7 7 2 0 1\n\nSecond number:5 8 2 6 3 7 3 5 2\n\nLet me write them stacked:\n\n        9 1 7 0 7 7 2 0 1\n\n      + 5 8 2 6 3 7 3 5 2\n\n      -----------------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nPosition0 (ones):1 +2=3\n\nPosition1 (tens):0 +5=5\n\nPosition2 (hundreds):2 +3=5\n\nPosition3 (thousands):7 +7=14 →4, carryover1\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):7 +3 +1=11 →1, carryover1\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands):0 +6 +1=7 →7, no carryover.\n\nPosition6 (millions):7 +2=9 →9, no carryover.\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):1 +8=9 →9, no carryover.\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):9 +5=14 →4, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (billions): carryover1.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nPosition9:1\n\nPosition8:4\n\nPosition7:9\n\nPosition6:9\n\nPosition5:7\n\nPosition4:1\n\nPosition3:4\n\nPosition2:5\n\nPosition1:5\n\nPosition0:3\n\nThus, the number is:\n\n1 (billions),\n\n4 (hundred millions),\n\n9 (ten millions),\n\n9 (millions),\n\n7 (hundred thousands),\n\n1 (ten thousands),\n\n4 (thousands),\n\n5 (hundreds),\n\n5 (tens),\n\n3 (ones).\n\nSo the number is 1,499,714,553?\n\nWait let's build it:\n\nBillions:1 →1,000,000,000\n\nHundred millions:4 →400,000,000 → total 1,400,000,000\n\nTen millions:9 →90,000,000 →1,490,000,000\n\nMillions:9 →9,000,000 →1,499,000,000\n\nHundred thousands:7 →700,000 →1,499,700,000\n\nTen thousands:1 →10,000 →1,499,710,000\n\nThousands:4 →4,000 →1,499,714,000\n\nHundreds:5 →500 →1,499,714,500\n\nTens:5 →50 →1,499,714,550\n\nOnes:3 →1,499,714,553.\n\nAh! Now this