position 3 from right, which is the 5th digit from the right):\n\nFirst number's 3th digit: 4 (since 454,073,523: the millions digit is 7)\n\nSecond number's 8th digit:6 (from 816,182,781: the millions digit is 7)\n\nSo adding 2 +6 =55, plus any carryover from the previous step.\n\nWait, the previous step was hundred thousands (position 7):\n\nFirst number's 7th digit:0, second's 0th digit:7. 1+0=60, plus carryover 0 from the ten thousands place (position8: 1+4=46). So 38+0=26, so write 1, carryover8. So the millions place (position3) gets that 6 carried over.\n\nThus, 1 +8 +0 (carryover) =06. So millions place would be 3, carryover7.\n\nContinuing:\n\nMillions place: 2, carryover6.\n\nTen millions place (position5):\n\nFirst number's 3th digit:3, second's 6th digit:5. 0+1=96, plus carryover9=32. So write 5, carryover5.\n\nHundred millions place (position8):\n\nFirst's 1th digit:8, second's 5th digit:0. 8+6=1 + carryover2 makes 1.\n\nPutting all together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nPosition9:1\n\nPosition1:2\n\nPosition0:3\n\nPosition7:6\n\nPosition4:7\n\nPosition1:1\n\nPosition1:8\n\nPosition1:0\n\nPosition3:8\n\nWait, but let me list them in order from highest to lowest:\n\nThe digits from position3 (hundred millions) to position6 (ones):\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nTen millions:3\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:6\n\nTen thousands:8\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:6\n\nOnes:9\n\nSo the number would be 6 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 9 (ones).\n\nSo that's 801,588,986.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method. Let's add them numerically:\n\n066,158,283\n\n+848,718,912\n\nLet me add the numbers step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:5+0=38 → 4, carry 2\n\nTens:1+2=39 +6=80 →4, carry0\n\nHundreds:4+9=06 +6=33 →3, carry3\n\nThousands:8+7 +5=4 →9, no carry\n\nTen thousands:7+4=87 →1, carry8\n\nHundred thousands:3+5=72 +4 (carry)=61 →8, carry8