) =4 → write4.\n\nThousands place:\n\n0 (first) +9 (second) → Wait, wait. Let me check the digits properly.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to write each number's digits correctly.\n\nWait, first number is 918,492,001:\n\nBreaking down each digit from right (ones) to left (billions):\n\nPosition1 (ones):1\n\nPosition2 (tens):0\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):0\n\nPosition4 (thousands):2\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):9\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):4\n\nPosition7 (millions):8\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):1\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):9\n\nSecond number:923,729,238\n\nDigits:\n\nPosition1 (ones):8\n\nPosition2 (tens):3\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):2\n\nPosition4 (thousands):9\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):2\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):7\n\nPosition7 (millions):3\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):2\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):9\n\nNow adding each position:\n\nPosition1 (ones):1+8=9 →9\n\nPosition2 (tens):0+3=3 →3\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):0+2=2 →2\n\nPosition4 (thousands):2+9=11 → write1, carryover1\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):9+2=11 +1 (carryover)=12 → write2, carryover1\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):4+7=11 +1=12 → write2, carryover1\n\nPosition7 (millions):8+3=11 +1=12 → write2, carryover1\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):1+2=3 +1=4 →4, no carryover.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):9+9=18 → write8, carryover1.\n\nNow the carryover1 from hundred millions goes to the next (billions) place:1.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\nBillions place:1,\n\nHundred millions:8,\n\nTen millions:4,\n\nMillions:2,\n\nHundred thousands:2,\n\nTen thousands:2,\n\nThousands:1,\n\nHundreds:2,\n\nTens:3,\n\nOnes:9.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\n1 (billions), 8 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 9 (ones).\n\nSo the number is 1,842,221,239.\n\nWait, but when I added the ten millions place: first number's ten millions is1, second's is2 →1+2=3 plus carryover1 from millions place (which was 12, so carryover1) → total 4. Correct.\n\nYes, so the final answer is 1,842,221,239.\n\nWait but let me check with a calculator:\n\n918,492,001 + 923,729,238.\n\nAdding 918,492,001 + 900,000,000 = 1,818,492,001.\n\nThen adding the remaining 23,729,238: 1,818,492,001 +23,729,238 = 1,842,221,239. Yes, that matches.\n\nTherefore the correct answer is 1,842,221,239.\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: 1 + 8 = 9\n2. The tens place: 0 + 3 = 3\n3. The hundreds place: 0 + 2 = 2\n4. The thousands place: 2 + 9 = 11 (write 1, carry over 1)\n5. The ten thousands place: 9 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 12 (write 2, carry over 1)\n6. The hundred thousands place: 4 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 12 (write 2, carry over 1)\n7. The millions place: 8 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 12 (write 2, carry over 1)\n8. The ten millions place: 1 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 4\n9. The hundred millions place: 9 + 9 = 18 (write 8, carry over 1)\n10. The billions place: 1 (carry)\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is 1842221239.", ''] 92%|#########2| 462/500 [3:53:41<33:56, 53.59s/it]
