next digit (since we've gone through all digits up to hundred millions).\n\nThus, the total digits are:\n\nBillions:0\n\nHundred millions:5\n\nTen millions:6\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:3\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:2\n\nPutting it all together from highest to lowest:\n\n4 (billions), 4 (hundred millions),3 (ten millions),1 (millions),3 (hundred thousands),5 (ten thousands),0 (thousands),0 (hundreds),8 (tens),0 (ones).\n\nWait, let me structure this properly:\n\nThe digits are:\n\nBillions place:5\n\nHundred millions:2\n\nTen millions:9\n\nMillions:9\n\nHundred thousands:1\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:8\n\nTens:3\n\nOnes:5\n\nSo the number is 5,796,224,816.\n\nWait, let's see:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n7,745,953,364\n\nYes, that's 0 billion, 00 million, 159 thousand, 950.\n\nWait, let me check if adding the two numbers directly gives the same:\n\n001,026,558\n\n+080,937,500\n\nLet's add them numerically:\n\n396,827,204\n\n+102,750,301\n\nStart adding:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1 +9=4\n\n7+2=35 (carry2)\n\n7+9+7=7\n\n1+6=6\n\n1+8=69 (carry2)\n\n9+7+0=68 (carry5)\n\n8+6+7=67 (carry3)\n\n7+1+9=71 (carry4)\n\n2+5+3=84 (carry0)\n\nThen the final carryover2.\n\nSo the sum is 9,805,579,310. That seems correct.\n\nWait, just to confirm, maybe use another method like rounding?\n\nAlternatively, approximate to check:\n\n975 million is roughly 156 million, 787 million is roughly 616 million. So total approx 9,483 million. The exact answer is 6,213 million, which is close, so that seems plausible.\n\nAnother way: 898,085,814 + 970,257,656.\n\nAdding the millions parts:\n\n715,489,840 is 075,011,424\n\n219,705,317 is 094,484,331\n\nAdding 494,146,578 + 889,313,284 = 006,853,553\n\nThen add 29,526,601: 160,541,573 +76,854,332.\n\n823,318,584 +14,157,429 = 7,925,983,807\n\nAdd 2,043,335: 3,821,016,430 +2,404,770 = ?\n\n3,518,969,375 +3,286,956 =0,229,551,268\n\nThen +394,047:\n\n4,293,052,449 + 032,188 =9,492,096,225\n\