s, 6 ten millions, 1 million). So the Ten-millions place addition is 1 (from first number) +6 (from second) =7. So no carryover here. \n\nLet me redo the entire calculation with corrected digits:\n\nStarting over with correct digits:\n\nNumbers:\n\nFirst number: 510,548,739 \u2192 digits from right (ones to hundred-millions):\n\nOnes:9, Tens:3, Hundreds:7, Thousands:8, Ten-thousands:4, Hundred-thousands:5, Millions:0, Ten-millions:1, Hundred-millions:5.\n\nSecond number:961,904,936 \u2192 digits:\n\nOnes:6, Tens:3, Hundreds:9, Thousands:4, Ten-thousands:0, Hundred-thousands:9, Millions:1, Ten-millions:6, Hundred-millions:9.\n\nNow step by step:\n\n**Ones place:**\n9 +6 =15 \u21925, carry 1\n\n**Tens place:**\n3 +3 +1 (carry)=7 \u21927, no carry\n\n**Hundreds place:**\n7 +9 =16 \u21926, carry1\n\n**Thousands place:**\n8 +4 +1 (carry)=13 \u21923, carry1\n\n**Ten-thousands place:**\n4 +0 +1 (carry)=5 \u21925, no carry\n\n**Hundred-thousands place:**\n5 +9 =14 \u21924, carry1\n\n**Millions place:**\n0 +1 +1 (carry)=2 \u21922, no carry\n\n**Ten-millions place:**\n1 +6 =7 \u21927, no carry\n\n**Hundred-millions place:**\n5 +9 =14 \u21924, carry1\n\nNow, since there are no higher digits, the carryover 1 from hundred-millions place becomes a new digit in the billions place.\n\nSo the final digits are:\n\nBillions place:1\n\nHundred-millions:4\n\nTen-millions:7\n\nMillions:2\n\nHundred-thousands:4\n\nTen-thousands:5\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:7\n\nOnes:5\n\nPutting it all together with commas:\n\n1,472,453,675\n\nWait, let's structure it properly:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred-millions:4 \u2192 1,400,000,000\n\nTen-millions:7 \u2192 1,470,000,000\n\nMillions:2 \u2192 1,472,000,000\n\nHundred-thousands:4 \u21921,472,400,000\n\nTen-thousands:5 \u21921,472,450,000\n\nThousands:3 \u21921,472,453,000\n\nHundreds:6 \u21921,472,453,600\n\nTens:7 \u21921,472,453,670\n\nOnes:5 \u21921,472,453,675\n\nTherefore, the correct sum is 1,472,453,675.\n\nNow, filling the template with this correct calculation:\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: 9 + 6 = 15. Write down 5, carry over 1.\n2. The tens place: 3 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 7. Write down 7.\n3. The hundreds place: 7 + 9 = 16. Write down 6, carry over 1.\n4. The thousands place: 8 + 4 + 1 (carry) = 13. Write down 3, carry over 1.\n5. The ten-thousands place: 4 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 5. Write down 5.\n6. The hundred-thousands place: 5 + 9 = 14. Write down 4, carry over 1.\n7. The millions place: 0 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 2. Write down 2.\n8. The ten-millions place: 1 + 6 = 7. Write down 7.\n9. The hundred-millions place: 5 + 9 = 14. Write down 4, carry over 1.\n10. The billions place: 1 (carry). Write down 1.\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is 1,472,453,675.",
