nThen 373 thousand +79 thousand =452 thousand.\n\n3861 +364 =4,225.\n\nSo total is 827,000,000 +452,000 =827,452,000 +4,225 =827,456,225. Wait, that's conflicting with previous result. Hmm, so there must be an error.\n\nWait let's compute again:\n\nWait 393,373,861 +434,079,364.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n393,373,861\n\n+434,079,364\n\n= ?\n\nLet's add the numbers in parts:\n\nFirst, add the millions:\n\n393,000,000 +434,000,000 =827,000,000\n\nThen the thousands:\n\n373,000 +79,000 =452,000\n\nThen the remaining:\n\n861 +364 =1,225\n\nAdding all together: 827,000,000 +452,000 =827,452,000 +1,225 =827,453,225.\n\nWait, so this is different from the previous digit-wise sum of 773,453,225. So there's a mistake in my first calculation.\n\nAh! I see where I messed up. Let me redo the digit-wise addition properly.\n\nFirst number:393,373,861\n\nSecond number:434,079,364\n\nAligning the digits:\n\nHundred millions Ten millions Millions Hundred thousands Ten thousands Thousands Hundreds Tens Ones\n\nFirst:3\u202f\u202f3\u202f\u202f9\u202f\u202f3\u202f\u202f7\u202f\u202f3\u202f\u202f8\u202f\u202f6\u202f\u202f1\n\nSecond:4\u202f\u202f3\u202f\u202f4\u202f\u202f0\u202f\u202f7\u202f\u202f9\u202f\u202f3\u202f\u202f6\u202f\u202f4\n\nAdding each column:\n\nOnes:1+4=5\n\nTens:6+6=12 →2, carryover1\n\nHundreds:8+3=11 +1=12 →2, carryover1\n\nThousands:3+9=12 +1=13 →3, carryover1\n\nTen thousands:7+7=14 +1=15 →5, carryover1\n\nHundred thousands:3+0=3 +1=4 →4, carryover0\n\nMillions:9+4=13 →3, carryover1\n\nTen millions:3+3=6 +1=7 →7, carryover0\n\nHundred millions:3+4=7 →7.\n\nWait so the digits are:\n\nOnes:5\n\nTens:2\n\nHundreds:2\n\nThousands:3\n\nTen thousands:5\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nMillions:3\n\nTen millions:7\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nSo the number is 7 (hundred millions),7 (ten millions),3 (millions),4 (hundred thousands),5 (ten thousands),3 (thousands),2 (hundreds),2 (tens),5 (ones).\n\nSo that's 773,453,225, but according to the other method it should be 827,453,225. \n\nAh! I