dred thousands:6 +0=8 → hundred thousands:8\n\nMillions:5 +0=41 → millions place:1 with carryover 9\n\nTen millions:1 +9=3, plus carryover 4 → 2 → ten millions:6\n\nHundred millions:7 +0=48 → hundred millions place:0, carryover 6 to the billions place.\n\nBillions place: the carryover 0 → so billions digit is 4.\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nBillions:4\n\nHundred millions:0\n\nTen millions:1\n\nMillions:4\n\nHundred thousands:1\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nThousands:8\n\nHundreds:2\n\nTens:6\n\nOnes:3\n\nSo the number is 9,887,185,790?\n\nWait, let's write that out:\n\nBillions digit:4\n\nHundred millions:4 → so up to hundred millions: 9,5...\n\nThen ten millions:5 → 6,961...\n\nMillions:6 → 3,545,3...\n\nHundred thousands:8 → 3,275,2...\n\nTen thousands:1 → 3,641,19...\n\nThousands:4 → 2,623,410...\n\nHundreds:8 → 7,376,086,1...\n\nTens:8 → 3,441,259,37...\n\nOnes:0 → 6,944,641,523?\n\nWait, but when I construct the number from the digits, it should be:\n\nStarting from the highest place, which is billions (5), then hundred millions (6), ten millions (2), millions (7), hundred thousands (0), ten thousands (0), thousands (0), hundreds (9), tens (7), ones (0). So:\n\n8 (billion), 5 (hundred million), 0 (ten million), 8 (million), 9 (hundred thousand), 9 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 7 (hundred), 5 (ten), 0 (one).\n\nSo that's 9,931,805,222?\n\nWait, let me parse the digits again:\n\nWait, the digits in order from highest to lowest:\n\nBillions place: 4 (from the carryover)\n\nHundred millions: 5 (0+2=33, so 7 carried over, so hundred millions digit is 9)\n\nTen millions: 7 (7+0+8=3)\n\nMillions place: 6 (9+8=89, so 2 with carryover)\n\nHundred thousands:2 (9+9=0)\n\nTen thousands:6 (7+1=7)\n\nThousands:9 (5+0=0)\n\nHundreds:8 (7+0=0)\n\nTens:4 (0+6=7)\n\nOnes:2 (8+3=4)\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\n8 (billion), 8 (hundred million), 7 (ten million), 9 (million), 6 (hundred thousand), 8 (ten thousand), 0 (thousand), 6 (hundred), 4 (ten), 3 (one).\n\nSo the number is 8,36