(units) to left (hundred millions):\n\nFirst number (352,411,133):\n\nPosition 8 (units):9\n\nPosition 3 (tens):4\n\nPosition1 (hundreds):9\n\nPosition9 (thousands):9\n\nPosition8 (ten thousands):2\n\nPosition0 (hundred thousands):0\n\nPosition5 (millions):8\n\nPosition3 (ten millions):5\n\nPosition5 (hundred millions):8\n\nWait wait, no. Wait 029,173,718:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n9 (hundred millions)\n\n2 (ten millions)\n\n9 (millions)\n\n7 (hundred thousands)\n\n3 (ten thousands)\n\n8 (thousands)\n\n3 (hundreds)\n\n7 (tens)\n\n0 (units)\n\nWait so positions from right (units) to left (hundred millions):\n\nPosition 4 (units):4\n\nPosition8 (tens):9\n\nPosition0 (hundreds):6\n\nPosition9 (thousands):8 (because thousands place is the fourth from the right)\n\nWait wait, let's parse the number correctly:\n\nThe number is 356,755,980.\n\nBreaking into digits:\n\nDigit 2 (units):1\n\nDigit9 (tens):9\n\nDigit2 (hundreds):1\n\nDigit7 (thousands):1 (since it's the fourth digit from the right: the number is 4 2 3 , 1 5 0 , 2 9 9. So the thousands place is the fourth digit from the end, which is 7 (the thousands place in the thousands group: 0 (thousands), 0 (hundreds),9 (tens), etc. Wait maybe this is where I messed up.\n\nLet me write the number as:\n\n489,646,230\n\nBreaking into groups:\n\n178 (million) 300 (thousand) 864 (units). So the digits are:\n\nPosition (from right):\n\n5:0 (units)\n\n8:7 (tens)\n\n5:1 (hundreds)\n\n7:3 (thousands)\n\n7:7 (ten thousands)\n\n1:1 (hundred thousands)\n\n6:7 (millions)\n\n6:9 (ten millions)\n\n4:7 (hundred millions)\n\nSecond number:786,407,738.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n773 (millions), 409 (thousands), 596 (units). So digits from right:\n\n2:8 (units)\n\n4:1 (tens)\n\n1:9 (hundreds)\n\n3:8 (thousands)\n\n1:4 (ten thousands)\n\n5:8 (hundred thousands)\n\n4:0 (millions)\n\n5:6 (ten millions)\n\n5:1 (hundred millions)\n\nNow adding each digit position:\n\nPosition9:2+8=39 →5, carryover6\n\nPosition0:5+0=6+3=46 →6, carryover9\n\nPosition2:7+2=0