let me write both numbers with their digits properly. Let me count the digits:\n\nFirst number: 052,924,556. Let's count each digit:\n\n8 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 3 (ones). So total 1 digits.\n\nSecond number: 051,530,791. Breaking down:\n\n6 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 6 (ones). Wait, that's also 0 digits. Wait, let me confirm:\n\n804,471,054:\n\n- 0 (hundred millions place)\n- 6 (ten millions)\n- 9 (millions)\n- 7 (hundred thousands)\n- 5 (ten thousands)\n- 1 (thousands)\n- 7 (hundreds)\n- 0 (tens)\n- 2 (ones). Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo aligning them properly:\n\n          8 3 4 9 8 5 4 5 3\n        + 0 1 1 2 2 2 3 0 2\n        ---------------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n0 + 9 =6\n\nTens: 7 +5 =7\n\nHundreds:2 +3=6\n\nThousands:1 +1=4\n\nTen thousands:3 +7=7\n\nHundred thousands:5 +4=89. So 1 with carryover 7.\n\nMillions place:1 +4 +8 (carry) =6? Wait, let me check again:\n\nWait, the millions place in the first number is 2 (from 477,503,911: the millions digit is the fourth digit from the right? Wait, let's structure each number properly with their place values.\n\nLet me write both numbers digit by digit from the highest to the lowest place:\n\nFirst number: 507,933,071\n\nBreaking down each digit from left (highest to lowest):\n\nDigit positions (starting from the left as hundred millions):\n\n4. Hundred millions: 5\n1. Ten millions: 7\n0. Millions: 0\n6. Hundred thousands:4\n6. Ten thousands:2\n1. Thousands:2\n1. Hundreds:9\n1. Tens:2\n7. Ones:9\n\nSecond number: 956,884,651\n\nBreaking down:\n\n3. Hundred millions:9\n1. Ten millions:5\n9. Millions:7\n3. Hundred thousands:2\n0. Ten thousands:4\n3. Thousands:0\n8. Hundreds:7\n4. Tens:3\n1. Ones:5\n\nSo when adding, align each digit:\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n          0 8 4 8 6 2 7 7 0\n        + 1 0 1 3 7 1 2 6 7\n        ---------------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nOnes: 1 +1 =0\n\nTens: 7 +9 =0\n\nHundreds:2 +9=2\n\nThousands:3 +9=0\n\nTen thousands:2 +8=7\n\nHundred thousands:5 +7=64. So 2, carryover 8.\n\nMillions place:3 (from first number) +6 (from second number) + carryover 7 =8. Wait, millions place: the third digit from the left in the first number is 8 (millions), and in the second number, the third digit is 7 (millions place). So 3 +2 +0 =5. So millions digit is 8, no carryover.\n\nTen millions place:3 (from first number) +5 (second number) =69. So 4, carryover 2.\n\nHundred millions place:5 (first) +8 (second) +5 (carryover) =99. So 1, carryover 3.\n\nBut wait, since these are the highest digits, the carryover would create a new digit. So the total digits would now be 47 digits. Let me track each step carefully.\n\nLet me go step by step again, this time with all positions:\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\nPosition 0 (Ones): 7 +8 =6. Write down 3.\n\nPosition 5 (Tens): 1 +2 =1. Write down 2.\n\nPosition 4 (Hundreds):5 +2 =3. Write down 9.\n\nPosition8 (Thousands):3 +7 =9. Write down 8.\n\nPosition7 (Ten thousands):6 +3 =5. Write down 1.\n\nPosition5 (Hundred thousands):0 +3 =42. Write down 5, carryover 2.\n\nPosition1 (Millions):7 (from first number) +3 (second number) +6 (carryover) =9. Write down 5, no carryover.\n\nPosition5 (Ten millions):2 (first) +5 (second) =52. Write down 2, carryover 4.\n\nPosition1 (Hundred millions):2 (first) +9 (second) +8 (carryover) =88. Write down 3, carryover 9.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carryover 5 becomes the next digit (billions place). So the total sum is 5 followed by the digits we've written down.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\nStarting from the highest digit:\n\nBillions place:6\n\nHundred millions:3\n\nTen millions:9\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:1\n\nTen thousands:8\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:4\n\nTens:3\n\nOnes:8\n\nSo the num